00:09:06,649 --> 00:09:08,789
-I can't believe they're
showing Dennis Franz's butt.

250
00:09:08,824 --> 00:09:11,412
-That ship must be
in outer space.

251
00:09:11,447 --> 00:09:13,760
-That's a toy
I wouldn't mind having.

252
00:09:13,794 --> 00:09:15,071
I like it very much.

253
00:09:15,106 --> 00:09:16,314
-Attention, people of Earth.

254
00:09:16,348 --> 00:09:17,591
-Ba-kawk.

255
00:09:17,626 --> 00:09:20,456
-I am Ambassador Phantom from
the planet Krankor.

256
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:22,078
-We are Ken.
-We are Ken.

257
00:09:22,113 --> 00:09:24,494
-I am rapidly approaching
your planet

258
00:09:24,529 --> 00:09:27,049
in the warship
which you have just seen.

259
00:09:27,083 --> 00:09:28,913
-Bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk.
-That's good.

260
00:09:28,947 --> 00:09:30,293
-It's overloading every channel.

261
00:09:30,328 --> 00:09:31,881
What a powerful beam
he must have.

262
00:09:31,916 --> 00:09:33,607
-Thank you.
-Look at that modulation.

263
00:09:33,642 --> 00:09:36,506
-I will arrive tomorrow night
at precisely 8:00.

264
00:09:36,541 --> 00:09:37,784
-Bawk, bawk.

265
00:09:37,818 --> 00:09:39,371
-At that time, I will make
my wishes known to you.

266
00:09:39,406 --> 00:09:40,338
-Bawk.

267
00:09:40,372 --> 00:09:42,512
-You will obey them or die.

268
00:09:42,547 --> 00:09:43,513
-Ba-kawk.

269
00:09:43,548 --> 00:09:45,136
-Have a pleasant night's sleep.

270
00:09:45,170 --> 00:09:47,483
[Laughs evilly]

271
00:09:47,517 --> 00:09:49,036
-How are you?

272
00:09:49,071 --> 00:09:50,590
-[Laughs evilly]

273
00:09:50,624 --> 00:09:52,488
-Krankor,
nothing to worry about.

274
00:09:52,522 --> 00:09:55,042
Truman Capote
sent to fight Krankor.

275
00:09:55,077 --> 00:09:57,976
[Horn honks]

276
00:09:58,011 --> 00:10:00,530
-Hey, there's Jerry
the reporter.

277
00:10:00,565 --> 00:10:01,670
-Hey, Wally.

278
00:10:01,704 --> 00:10:03,119
-What is it, Beav?

279
00:10:03,154 --> 00:10:05,018
-Hot off the press.

280
00:10:05,052 --> 00:10:05,915
-Thanks.

281
00:10:05,950 --> 00:10:07,192
Where are you going?

282
00:10:07,227 --> 00:10:09,505
-Professor Macken is giving
a press conference.

283
00:10:09,539 --> 00:10:11,645
-He's supposed to know
what these spacemen want.

284
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,198
He might know how
we can fight them off too.

285
00:10:13,233 --> 00:10:15,407
-Yeah. Got a whole bunch
of firecrackers

286
00:10:15,442 --> 00:10:17,099
left over from last year.

287
00:10:17,133 --> 00:10:18,203
Maybe we can use them.

288
00:10:18,238 --> 00:10:19,480
[Laughter]

289
00:10:19,515 --> 00:10:20,758
-Let's go. We're late now.
-Goodbye.

290
00:10:20,792 --> 00:10:21,759
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye!

291
00:10:21,793 --> 00:10:24,762
-Goodbye, unfunny, weird man.

292
00:10:24,796 --> 00:10:26,384
-He seems like a real jerk.

293
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:29,111
-Say, Wally, I bet you're
afraid of those spacemen.

294
00:10:29,145 --> 00:10:30,630
-Of course I am.
-What for?

295
00:10:30,664 --> 00:10:31,941
You aren't going to be much help

296
00:10:31,976 --> 00:10:33,943
if you get frightened
as easy as that.

297
00:10:33,978 --> 00:10:36,290
-I'm not here.

298
00:10:36,325 --> 00:10:38,051
-Walter Mondale arrives.

299
00:10:38,879 --> 00:10:40,363
-Come on, fellas.
Shake a leg, we're late.

300
00:10:40,398 --> 00:10:42,745
-I have to swing in
for some violent porn comics.

301
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,989
-Where is he?
-Oh, here he comes now.

302
00:10:45,023 --> 00:10:45,921
Good morning, professor.

303
00:10:45,955 --> 00:10:47,992
-It's the subway fondler club.

304
00:10:48,026 --> 00:10:49,200
-Good morning, gentlemen.

305
00:10:49,234 --> 00:10:50,684
-Welcome to
my grandma's living room.

306
00:10:50,719 --> 00:10:52,306
-Well, now,
do you have any questions?

307
00:10:52,341 --> 00:10:53,411
-Yes, professor.

308
00:10:53,445 --> 00:10:54,723
What about these spacemen, sir?

309
00:10:54,757 --> 00:10:57,070
Do we expect them
to attempt to land here?

310
00:10:57,104 --> 00:10:58,934
-Yes. Let me explain.

311
00:10:58,968 --> 00:11:00,107
You know, gentlemen,

312
00:11:00,142 --> 00:11:02,109
we have developed
a powerful new rocket fuel.

313
00:11:02,144 --> 00:11:03,283
-Mm-hmm.
-Yes, sir.

314
00:11:03,317 --> 00:11:05,216
-Now for reasons
which must remain classified,

315
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:06,355
we believe their visit

316
00:11:06,389 --> 00:11:07,563
has something to do
with this discovery.

317
00:11:07,597 --> 00:11:08,978
-Wait a minute, professor.

318
00:11:09,013 --> 00:11:11,463
These people are obviously
much more advanced than we are.

319
00:11:11,498 --> 00:11:13,224
What could they possibly want
from us?

320
00:11:13,258 --> 00:11:15,605
-Yes, they've already achieved
interplanetary space travel.

321
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,918
That's more than we have, sir.

322
00:11:17,953 --> 00:11:18,954
-Oh...

323
00:11:18,988 --> 00:11:20,472
-Oh, it seems
that you are right,

324
00:11:20,507 --> 00:11:22,198
at least about space travel.

325
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:24,856
In another respect,
in the question of fuel,

326
00:11:24,891 --> 00:11:27,445
their technology lags
far behind ours.

327
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:28,515
Now if they were capable

328
00:11:28,549 --> 00:11:30,828
of producing a rocket fuel
like mine,

329
00:11:30,862 --> 00:11:34,314
why, they could send 100 ships
to Earth instead of one.

330
00:11:34,348 --> 00:11:38,214
They could conquer
the entire world in a week.

331
00:11:38,249 --> 00:11:39,353
-Thank you very much
and goodbye.

332
00:11:39,388 --> 00:11:41,770
-The Japanese Don Knotts.

333
00:11:41,804 --> 00:11:43,633
-Oh, Jerry, there you are.

334
00:11:43,668 --> 00:11:44,669
-Jerry, baby.

335
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:46,360
-Very good story,
both of you.

336
00:11:46,395 --> 00:11:48,466
I'm giving you bylines
on the front page.

337
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,813
-I hope there will be
someone around to read it.

338
00:11:50,848 --> 00:11:52,504
We've just come
from the war office.

339
00:11:52,539 --> 00:11:54,058
They're declaring
a general alert.

340
00:11:54,092 --> 00:11:55,335
-Oh, a general alert?

341
00:11:55,369 --> 00:11:56,612
-Does it affect my bow tie?

342
00:11:56,646 --> 00:11:57,717
-This must be serious.

343
00:11:58,890 --> 00:12:00,685
-They're going
to try to land here?

344
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,445
-Well, it's not official,

345
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:04,309
but they're heading this way
for sure.

346
00:12:04,344 --> 00:12:05,379
-Is that right?

347
00:12:05,414 --> 00:12:07,796
-They're coming here then.

348
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:09,038
-You're fascinating.

349
00:12:09,073 --> 00:12:11,178
-Gentlemen, this may be
our last day on Earth.

350
00:12:11,213 --> 00:12:12,455
-Let's hit the karaoke bar.

351
00:12:12,490 --> 00:12:14,388
-Whoo.

352
00:12:14,423 --> 00:12:16,839
♪♪

353
00:12:16,874 --> 00:12:19,393
-A rare Godzilla-free day.

354
00:12:19,428 --> 00:12:21,326
♪♪

355
00:12:21,361 --> 00:12:23,570
-This is Metropolitan Police
speaking,

356
00:12:23,604 --> 00:12:25,020
Metropolitan Police speaking.

357
00:12:25,054 --> 00:12:26,607
-♪ Ding-ding, ding-ding,
ding-ding, ding-ding ♪

358
00:12:26,642 --> 00:12:29,438
-All persons are warned 
to stay off the streets.

359
00:12:29,472 --> 00:12:32,855
All persons are warned 
to stay off the streets.

360
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:34,236
-Paging Mr. Herman.

361
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:37,480
-Civil defense personnel 
report to their stations.

362
00:12:37,515 --> 00:12:40,518
Civil defense personnel 
report to their stations.

363
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:41,415
-Come on.

364
00:12:41,450 --> 00:12:43,176
-All others take shelter.

365
00:12:43,210 --> 00:12:44,971
All other persons take shelter.

366
00:12:45,005 --> 00:12:46,248
Do not panic.

367
00:12:46,282 --> 00:12:47,525
Follow instructions.

368
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:49,285
You will not get hurt.

369
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:53,634
-[Humming tune from
"Firesign Theatre"]

370
00:12:53,669 --> 00:12:55,395
-Regional control reporting.

371
00:12:55,429 --> 00:12:57,811
All metropolitan sections 
are on red alert.

372
00:12:57,846 --> 00:13:00,780
Repeat, a little metropolitan 
sections are on red alert.

373
00:13:00,814 --> 00:13:03,575
Over and out.

374
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:04,645
-Stop looking at us.

375
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,717
Mind your own business.

376
00:13:07,752 --> 00:13:09,167
-I wonder where Wally is.

377
00:13:09,202 --> 00:13:10,410
He said he would come tonight.

378
00:13:10,444 --> 00:13:11,480
-Uh-huh.

379
00:13:11,514 --> 00:13:13,862
-He's got some stones
to mess with me.

380
00:13:13,896 --> 00:13:15,829
-Monet in Paris.

381
00:13:15,864 --> 00:13:17,693
[Dog barking]

382
00:13:17,727 --> 00:13:19,626
-A ruff-a-roo, bow-a-wow.

383
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:20,627
[Dog barking]

384
00:13:20,661 --> 00:13:21,973
-After that dog!

385
00:13:24,734 --> 00:13:29,187
-♪ Where is aruff?

386
00:13:29,222 --> 00:13:33,260
-[Laughs]

387
00:13:33,295 --> 00:13:34,883
-One minute to 8:00.

388
00:13:34,917 --> 00:13:37,264
Is your watch right?

389
00:13:37,299 --> 00:13:39,680
[Buzzing]

390
00:13:39,715 --> 00:13:41,855
-Listen, here they come.

391
00:13:41,890 --> 00:13:43,167
-Is his watch right?

392
00:13:43,201 --> 00:13:44,306
We may never know.

393
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:45,169
-Come on.

394
00:13:45,203 --> 00:13:46,756
[Buzzing continues]

395
00:13:46,791 --> 00:13:49,276
-Can you see anything?

396
00:13:49,311 --> 00:13:51,347
-[Gasps] The Sony blimp.

397
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:54,419
-There. Look, over there!

398
00:13:54,454 --> 00:13:55,973
-It's Cheap Trick.

399
00:13:59,390 --> 00:14:01,841
-Surrender, Dorothy.

400
00:14:03,912 --> 00:14:06,431
-Same goes for you, Paris.

401
00:14:08,192 --> 00:14:09,952
-Pagoda of the damned.

402
00:14:09,987 --> 00:14:12,299
[Buzzing]

403
00:14:12,334 --> 00:14:15,751
-An alien race too proud
to ask for directions.

404
00:14:15,785 --> 00:14:18,581
-My baby sun hat and smock
will protect me.

405
00:14:22,723 --> 00:14:25,209
-Protect me, Japanese Fabian.

406
00:14:29,661 --> 00:14:31,284
-Chief.
-What?

407
00:14:31,318 --> 00:14:32,423
-I've just got a report

408
00:14:32,457 --> 00:14:33,838
about some strange
electrical disturbance

409
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,046
out near Beaver Falls.

410
00:14:35,081 --> 00:14:36,047
-You did?

411
00:14:36,082 --> 00:14:37,083
-Beaver Falls?

412
00:14:37,117 --> 00:14:38,256
-Better get out there
right away,

413
00:14:38,291 --> 00:14:39,395
and take a photographer
with you.

414
00:14:39,430 --> 00:14:40,672
-Oh, let me go too, chief.
All right?

415
00:14:40,707 --> 00:14:41,777
Hmm?
-Yeah.

416
00:14:41,811 --> 00:14:43,572
-Go, you bizarre little man.

417
00:14:44,469 --> 00:14:46,126
-Well, consider yourself
conquered.

418
00:14:46,161 --> 00:14:47,196
I got to go.

419
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:54,238
♪♪

420
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:58,069
-Beaver Falls Control here,
UFO descending in area 220.

421
00:14:58,104 --> 00:14:59,105
-All right. Let's go.

422
00:14:59,139 --> 00:15:00,037
-Okay.

423
00:15:00,071 --> 00:15:01,901
Uh, yeah, let's go.

424
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,351
-♪ Ohh

425
00:15:04,386 --> 00:15:06,215
-♪ Here we go off
to Beaver Falls ♪

426
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:08,079
♪ Beaver Falls, Beaver Falls

427
00:15:08,114 --> 00:15:09,943
♪ Here we go off
to Beaver Falls ♪

428
00:15:09,978 --> 00:15:11,841
♪ Early in the morning

429
00:15:14,465 --> 00:15:16,536
-I burned my tofu.

430
00:15:17,813 --> 00:15:18,952
-Something over there.
-Right.

431
00:15:18,987 --> 00:15:20,126
Maintain radio contact
with headquarters.

432
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:21,334
-Right.

433
00:15:21,368 --> 00:15:24,026
-Ah, the Stanley Cup
has invaded Earth, hmm?

434
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,753
-Aliens, come here right now.

435
00:15:26,787 --> 00:15:28,065
-No, wait.

436
00:15:28,099 --> 00:15:29,514
It's a periscope.

437
00:15:29,549 --> 00:15:31,033
-Deploy your men around it.
-Right.

438
00:15:32,138 --> 00:15:36,314
-I am the lemon zester
of destruction.

439
00:15:36,349 --> 00:15:37,660
[Indistinct conversations]

440
00:15:37,695 --> 00:15:38,972
-Bok choy. Wasabi.

441
00:15:39,007 --> 00:15:41,837
-Samurai.
-Wasabi.

442
00:15:41,871 --> 00:15:43,701
-Hey, there's Macken's car.

443
00:15:43,735 --> 00:15:45,220
[Indistinct conversations]

444
00:15:45,254 --> 00:15:47,360
-That's a lot more interesting
than a spaceship, a car!

445
00:15:47,394 --> 00:15:49,362
-Look, he brought his kids
with him.

446
00:15:49,396 --> 00:15:51,467
-Hey, Professor Macken,
you're just in time.

447
00:15:51,502 --> 00:15:52,952
The spaceship
just landed over here.

448
00:15:52,986 --> 00:15:54,298
-Yes, I know.

449
00:15:54,332 --> 00:15:55,782
Well, what's going on?
Who's in charge here?

450
00:15:55,816 --> 00:15:58,060
-The commissioner himself,but he's up there investigating.

451
00:15:58,095 --> 00:15:59,993
-Oh, I see.
[Indistinct conversations]

452
00:16:00,028 --> 00:16:03,445
-Sir, your office called.

453
00:16:03,479 --> 00:16:04,722
-Hmm, David Byrne.

454
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:07,414
♪♪

455
00:16:07,449 --> 00:16:09,002
-Hello?

456
00:16:09,037 --> 00:16:10,590
Hello?
-Hello?

457
00:16:10,624 --> 00:16:12,454
-Hello?
-Hello?

458
00:16:12,488 --> 00:16:16,285
[Drum rhythm plays]
-What message speaks the drums?

459
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,047
-Junior Samples
and Business Boy.

460
00:16:19,081 --> 00:16:20,151
-What's the matter with you,
Mickey?

461
00:16:20,186 --> 00:16:21,290
This might be dangerous.

462
00:16:21,325 --> 00:16:23,396
-I'm not afraid.
If you are, go on home.

463
00:16:23,430 --> 00:16:25,398
-Wait, those are
two separate ideas.

464
00:16:25,432 --> 00:16:26,813
-Yeah.

465
00:16:33,302 --> 00:16:35,787
-What?

466
00:16:35,822 --> 00:16:37,203
-Oh.

467
00:16:37,237 --> 00:16:38,998
-It's a giant watermelon.

468
00:16:39,032 --> 00:16:40,447
Gallagher is taking over.

469
00:16:40,482 --> 00:16:41,414
-Oh!
-Oh!

470
00:16:41,448 --> 00:16:43,140
-Forward.

471
00:16:43,174 --> 00:16:44,969
-Okay, good luck, sir.
Let me know what...

472
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:46,695
Oh, you want me to go with you.

473
00:16:46,729 --> 00:16:47,592
[Zap]

474
00:16:47,627 --> 00:16:50,043
[All scream]

475
00:16:50,078 --> 00:16:51,148
-I saw some smoke.

476
00:16:51,182 --> 00:16:52,701
It's time for lunch.
Look at this tree.

477
00:16:52,735 --> 00:16:54,496
-Look, he destroyed them
completely.

478
00:16:54,530 --> 00:16:57,775
-Except for their salad bowls!

479
00:16:57,809 --> 00:17:00,364
-Men of Earth, 
this is my first warning.

480
00:17:00,398 --> 00:17:03,746
Do not attempt to come nearer, 
or you will be destroyed.

481
00:17:03,781 --> 00:17:07,854
Obey my orders. 
You are warned.

482
00:17:07,888 --> 00:17:09,994
-That is one crafty
parking meter.

483
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,306
-Good lord.

484
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:12,548
-Get back to the car.

485
00:17:12,583 --> 00:17:14,481
Notify the defense ministry.
-Right.

486
00:17:14,516 --> 00:17:16,518
-Remember to crack a window.

487
00:17:16,552 --> 00:17:18,520
-Oh, hi, Dave.
You here too?

488
00:17:18,554 --> 00:17:19,590
[Zaps]

489
00:17:19,624 --> 00:17:21,281
[All shout]

490
00:17:21,316 --> 00:17:22,627
-I'm not afraid.
I'm wearing a tie.

491
00:17:22,662 --> 00:17:23,663
You go home.

492
00:17:23,697 --> 00:17:25,630
-Inspector. Inspector!

493
00:17:25,665 --> 00:17:27,011
-Where are you?
What happened?

494
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:30,083
-Inspector!
-Look, Commissioner.

495
00:17:30,118 --> 00:17:31,912
This is his gun.

496
00:17:31,947 --> 00:17:33,052
-Follow me.

497
00:17:33,086 --> 00:17:34,570
-Wet them if you've got them.

498
00:17:35,502 --> 00:17:37,021
-Take cover.
It's dangerous.

499
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:38,540
Radio car, get the
defense ministry quick!

500
00:17:38,574 --> 00:17:40,300
-What happened over there?
-The police force was attacked,

501
00:17:40,335 --> 00:17:42,647
some kind of a death ray.

502
00:17:42,682 --> 00:17:44,270
-What's that over there?
Look!

503
00:17:44,304 --> 00:17:45,478
[Indistinct conversations]

504
00:17:45,512 --> 00:17:46,755
-Oh!
-Oh!

505
00:17:46,789 --> 00:17:47,963
-[Gasps]
-Oh!

506
00:17:47,997 --> 00:17:49,102
-Hey, what's that?

507
00:17:49,137 --> 00:17:50,586
-Looks like a flying saucer.

508
00:17:50,621 --> 00:17:52,692
-Looks more like an upside down
flying wheelbarrow

509
00:17:52,726 --> 00:17:55,833
with a stupa on top,
but I guess you could think --

510
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:58,456
[Buzzing]

511
00:17:58,491 --> 00:18:01,010
-Oh, it's Buggy the spaceship.

512
00:18:05,498 --> 00:18:06,809
[Crash]

513
00:18:06,844 --> 00:18:08,466
-Holy Santa, pray for us.

514
00:18:12,056 --> 00:18:14,196
-Ha, made you duck.

515
00:18:16,681 --> 00:18:18,994
-What is that thing?
You go home. Hats are good.

516
00:18:21,169 --> 00:18:22,480
-Hello.

517
00:18:22,515 --> 00:18:25,414
-"Grown-Ups of the Corn."

518
00:18:25,449 --> 00:18:28,521
-Mitch Gaylord.
-[Chuckles]

519
00:18:28,555 --> 00:18:30,178
-What's that, a man?
-Mm-hmm.

520
00:18:30,212 --> 00:18:32,076
-Yeah, believe it or not, yup.

521
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,699
[Fanfare plays]

522
00:18:34,734 --> 00:18:37,150
-The king approaches!

523
00:18:37,185 --> 00:18:40,015
-Phantom of Krankor,
hear my words.

524
00:18:40,049 --> 00:18:42,328
I warn you to leave this planet.

525
00:18:42,362 --> 00:18:43,777
You are not wanted here.

526
00:18:43,812 --> 00:18:46,849
I warn you for the last time.

527
00:18:46,884 --> 00:18:48,748
-And by the last,
I mean first.

528
00:18:53,339 --> 00:18:56,445
-I have no powers,
but I can skip reasonably well.

529
00:18:59,655 --> 00:19:02,348
-Your weapons are useless 
against me, Phantom.

530
00:19:02,382 --> 00:19:05,351
You are merely exhausting 
your energy supply.

531
00:19:05,385 --> 00:19:07,560
You must leave the Earth 
at once.

532
00:19:07,594 --> 00:19:09,044
-All right.
Let me talk to him.

533
00:19:09,078 --> 00:19:10,252
-Who are you?

534
00:19:10,287 --> 00:19:12,392
Get him on the televisor, quick!

535
00:19:12,427 --> 00:19:14,360
-But I'm spinning my salad.

536
00:19:14,394 --> 00:19:15,499
-It is enough that I know you.

537
00:19:15,533 --> 00:19:16,810
You are Phantom of Krankor,

538
00:19:16,845 --> 00:19:18,191
and you wish 
to rule the universe.

539
00:19:18,226 --> 00:19:20,055
-He's going to get grass stains
on his dance skins.

540
00:19:20,089 --> 00:19:22,230
-You are planning now
to destroy the whole world.

541
00:19:22,264 --> 00:19:23,990
I won't let you go through
with this.

542
00:19:24,024 --> 00:19:25,612
You will not get 
what you've come for.

543
00:19:25,647 --> 00:19:27,407
You might as well leave now.

544
00:19:27,442 --> 00:19:30,376
-But who are you?
Tell me.

545
00:19:30,410 --> 00:19:31,618
Who are you? 
What's your name?

546
00:19:31,653 --> 00:19:33,827
-I am Prince of Space.

547
00:19:33,862 --> 00:19:35,208
-[Gasps]
-Whoo-hoo! Hoo-hoo!

548
00:19:35,243 --> 00:19:37,072
-Wait a moment.

549
00:19:37,106 --> 00:19:39,488
-Larry, we got anything
on this Prince of Space guy?

550
00:19:39,523 --> 00:19:40,593
[Buzzing]

551
00:19:40,627 --> 00:19:42,388
[Beeping]

552
00:19:42,422 --> 00:19:45,425
-Powered by rotted fish,
I will defeat you.

553
00:19:47,703 --> 00:19:49,498
-My contacts is bothering me.

554
00:19:52,639 --> 00:19:54,503
-Captain, look
at the atom machine.

555
00:19:54,538 --> 00:19:56,333
-The plutonium
is going critical, sir.

556
00:19:56,367 --> 00:19:57,541
-Keep shooting.

557
00:19:57,575 --> 00:19:59,267
You will overload 
your power supply.

558
00:19:59,301 --> 00:20:01,579
-We have to place
the lunch order, sir.

559
00:20:01,614 --> 00:20:02,580
-He's right.

560
00:20:02,615 --> 00:20:03,823
We better quit.

561
00:20:03,857 --> 00:20:05,169
We won't have enough power
to give back.

562
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,378
-Right.
We had better give up now.

563
00:20:07,413 --> 00:20:09,242
-Shall I prepare
for takeoff, sir?

564
00:20:09,277 --> 00:20:10,864
-Make it ba-kawk.

565
00:20:10,899 --> 00:20:13,522
♪♪

566
00:20:13,557 --> 00:20:15,110
-Though I can easily
defeat them, I must get away.

567
00:20:15,144 --> 00:20:16,698
Mom!

568
00:20:16,732 --> 00:20:18,217
♪♪

569
00:20:18,251 --> 00:20:20,322
-Hey, Mickey, let's get back
with the others now.

570
00:20:20,357 --> 00:20:21,634
-All right.

571
00:20:21,668 --> 00:20:22,911
-Any by the way,
you're so fine, hey, Mickey.

572
00:20:22,945 --> 00:20:24,499
-They're taking off.
-Get them out of here.

573
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:25,879
-Get clear of the rocket blast.

574
00:20:25,914 --> 00:20:27,295
Everybody, get back.

575
00:20:27,329 --> 00:20:30,229
-Back to your 3x5 apartments,
men.

576
00:20:30,263 --> 00:20:31,678
[Buzzing]

577
00:20:31,713 --> 00:20:33,093
-A stand of cedars.

578
00:20:33,128 --> 00:20:34,405
A spaceship is taking off.

579
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,751
And I am tired.

580
00:20:35,786 --> 00:20:37,926
-It's a haiku.
-That's nice.

581
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,272
-Thank you.

582
00:20:39,307 --> 00:20:40,929
-Into my modified pith helmet.

583
00:20:44,173 --> 00:20:46,245
-Get the emergency
reserve power working.

584
00:20:46,279 --> 00:20:47,418
-Yes, sir.

585
00:20:47,453 --> 00:20:48,661
-I'm going to kill
this Prince of Space

586
00:20:48,695 --> 00:20:50,283
if it's the last thing I do.

587
00:20:50,318 --> 00:20:53,907
-There goes a narwhal.

588
00:20:53,942 --> 00:20:57,083
-So what? Is he escorting them
to the county line?

589
00:20:57,117 --> 00:21:00,328
-Mom says I have to wear this
in space because it's cold.

590
00:21:03,779 --> 00:21:06,472
-We're ready to shoot, sir.
-Stand by to fire.

591
00:21:06,506 --> 00:21:08,957
-Let him get a little closer.
We can't miss.

592
00:21:11,442 --> 00:21:13,548
-Bawk.

593
00:21:13,582 --> 00:21:15,101
♪♪

594
00:21:15,135 --> 00:21:17,759
-He's Prince of watching
his space cushion.

595
00:21:17,793 --> 00:21:19,519
♪♪

596
00:21:19,554 --> 00:21:23,316
-Good spaceship
and a good, close shave.

597
00:21:23,351 --> 00:21:25,491
-I'm going to turn on the air.
Anybody mind?

598
00:21:25,525 --> 00:21:27,182
[Beeping]

599
00:21:27,216 --> 00:21:29,736
-Twenty thousand leagues
above the sea.

600
00:21:32,705 --> 00:21:37,019
-Wow, an exchange of
deadly negative scratches.

601
00:21:40,713 --> 00:21:42,231
-Why don't we take lunch now?

602
00:21:42,266 --> 00:21:43,888
-He's still coming on.

603
00:21:45,994 --> 00:21:47,202
-It's a pretty good war,

604
00:21:47,236 --> 00:21:49,584
but I'm going to
swing it around, yup.

605
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:54,140
-You there,
discharge the caustic vapors.

606
00:21:54,174 --> 00:21:55,797
-Yeah, look who's talking.

607
00:21:57,937 --> 00:22:00,698
-Engage the musical saw.

608
00:22:00,733 --> 00:22:04,150
[Whirring]

609
00:22:04,184 --> 00:22:06,048
-It's a cloud of fish oil.

610
00:22:06,083 --> 00:22:09,983
♪♪

611
00:22:10,018 --> 00:22:11,364
-Is that Ron?

612
00:22:11,399 --> 00:22:13,193
-Hmm.

613
00:22:13,228 --> 00:22:14,850
-you know, if the aliens
got new spark plugs,

614
00:22:14,885 --> 00:22:17,784
they'd get
a lot better mileage.

615
00:22:17,819 --> 00:22:20,200
-I see that their ship
totally let one.

616
00:22:20,235 --> 00:22:24,066
♪♪

617
00:22:24,101 --> 00:22:27,207
-Japanese are franticallytrying to pick up "Singled Out."

618
00:22:29,382 --> 00:22:32,523
-Humiliating game shows
are beamed across the nation.

619
00:22:34,870 --> 00:22:36,320
-Gentlemen, as you are aware,

620
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:38,909
our national territory was
invaded by an enemy last night.

621
00:22:38,943 --> 00:22:40,117
-Bingo here!

622
00:22:40,151 --> 00:22:41,498
-He was able to paralyze
our radar stations

623
00:22:41,532 --> 00:22:44,328
and move at will
through our national skies.

624
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:46,088
He was eventually driven off
single-handed

625
00:22:46,123 --> 00:22:48,470
by the pilot of
an unidentified flying saucer.

626
00:22:48,505 --> 00:22:49,989
-Bingo!

627
00:22:50,023 --> 00:22:51,818
-All we know is that this pilot
calls himself Prince of Space,

628
00:22:51,853 --> 00:22:53,648
but as to who he is,
where he has come from,

629
00:22:53,682 --> 00:22:55,788
or why he has fought our enemy,
we have no information.

630
00:22:55,822 --> 00:22:56,996
-Buh-buh-buh-bing.

631
00:22:57,030 --> 00:22:59,032
-We do know, however,
that after the battle,

632
00:22:59,067 --> 00:23:01,690
the flying saucer was seen
returning to this area,

633
00:23:01,725 --> 00:23:05,142
and we believe it is
still in this area now.

634
00:23:05,176 --> 00:23:06,592
-Hi.
-Hello.

635
00:23:06,626 --> 00:23:07,731
Late this morning?

636
00:23:07,765 --> 00:23:09,767
-Last night,
what happened to you?

637
00:23:09,802 --> 00:23:11,010
-Last night?

638
00:23:11,044 --> 00:23:12,736
Oh, an old friend asked me
to go out to dinner.

639
00:23:12,770 --> 00:23:14,220
-Hey, Wally, you missed it.

640
00:23:14,254 --> 00:23:16,222
I saw Prince of Space
last night.

641
00:23:16,256 --> 00:23:17,257
He chased away the spacemen.

642
00:23:17,292 --> 00:23:18,086
-I like the kid.

643
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:19,190
-Oh?

644
00:23:19,225 --> 00:23:20,606
-Here's the whole story
right here.

645
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,884
You can read
in this morning's paper.

646
00:23:22,918 --> 00:23:25,265
-Listen, Wally, do you think
that Prince of Space

647
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,750
really comes from the stars?

648
00:23:26,784 --> 00:23:28,924
-I guess so.
-Thank you.

649
00:23:28,959 --> 00:23:30,926
-Why not?
What do you think?

650
00:23:30,961 --> 00:23:33,619
The Prince of Space
might just be a man like Wally?

651
00:23:33,653 --> 00:23:34,999
-Woody Allen asked me out.

652
00:23:35,034 --> 00:23:37,692
-Well, in a way he is,
if you think about it.

653
00:23:37,726 --> 00:23:39,728
After all,
I believe in peace too.

654
00:23:39,763 --> 00:23:41,903
I would be willing to fight
this Phantom character

655
00:23:41,937 --> 00:23:43,491
same way as he did.

656
00:23:43,525 --> 00:23:45,631
-You wouldn't fight him.
You were too scared.

657
00:23:45,665 --> 00:23:47,322
-Are we going to work
at all today?

658
00:23:47,356 --> 00:23:48,737
-I better be going now.
-Going where?

659
00:23:48,772 --> 00:23:50,049
-Over to Johnnie's house.

660
00:23:50,083 --> 00:23:52,569
I made him promise to keep
watching the telescope.

661
00:23:52,603 --> 00:23:53,811
-Let's go to Johnnie's house.

662
00:23:53,846 --> 00:23:55,157
-Maybe this Phantom
will come back here again.

663
00:23:55,192 --> 00:23:56,538
-I like it very much.

664
00:23:56,573 --> 00:23:58,229
-Kimmy, you stay with Wally.

665
00:24:10,587 --> 00:24:12,520
-Oh, yeah, Mike,
I was wondering that myself.

666
00:24:12,554 --> 00:24:13,762
Weird, isn't it?

667
00:24:13,797 --> 00:24:14,832
-Oh, hey, Tom.

668
00:24:14,867 --> 00:24:15,764
How did you get here so fast?

669
00:24:15,799 --> 00:24:17,007
-Oh, he'll be along.

670
00:24:17,041 --> 00:24:18,871
I have his chicken puppet.
-Hey, where's Crow?

671
00:24:18,905 --> 00:24:20,113
-Talking like what?

672
00:24:20,148 --> 00:24:21,598
-Why are you talking like that?
-No, I'm not.

673
00:24:21,632 --> 00:24:23,807
I'm just way ahead of you, Mike.-Well, like that.

674
00:24:23,841 --> 00:24:25,947
You know, you're answering
my questions before I ask them.

675
00:24:25,981 --> 00:24:27,673
I don't know, I'm just
asking him the same thing.

676
00:24:27,707 --> 00:24:29,157
-No, you dope.

677
00:24:29,191 --> 00:24:31,331
I mean, I'm moving faster
than you temporally speaking.

678
00:24:31,366 --> 00:24:32,954
-Hey, what do you mean
you're way ahead of me?

679
00:24:32,988 --> 00:24:33,955
-Well, I asked you
for it, Crow.

680
00:24:33,989 --> 00:24:36,095
You were right here.
-Hi, guys.

681
00:24:36,129 --> 00:24:38,028
Hey, how did you
get here so fast?

682
00:24:38,062 --> 00:24:39,374
-That's what I've been trying
to tell you, Mike.

683
00:24:39,408 --> 00:24:40,824
I'm ahead of you
by about 3 seconds.

684
00:24:40,858 --> 00:24:42,066
-You know what, guys?

685
00:24:42,101 --> 00:24:42,964
I think there may be
something wrong

686
00:24:42,998 --> 00:24:45,000
with the space-time continuum.

687
00:24:45,035 --> 00:24:46,726
-Servo, how did you get
my chicken puppet?

688
00:24:46,761 --> 00:24:47,900
-Nope, sorry.

689
00:24:47,934 --> 00:24:49,280
Everything is on the fritz.

690
00:24:49,315 --> 00:24:51,351
My burrito was done
before I put it in the oven.

691
00:24:51,386 --> 00:24:53,353
-All right, all right.
Take your damn chicken puppet.

692
00:24:53,388 --> 00:24:55,528
I'll have it back
before you know it anyway.

693
00:24:55,563 --> 00:24:56,633
-Hey, Tom, why don't you just

694
00:24:56,667 --> 00:24:58,186
give him his chicken puppet
back, all right?

695
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:00,464
-Say, why don't we ask Gypsy
to mess with the warp engine?

696
00:25:00,499 --> 00:25:03,916
-Well, alls I know is I want
my chicken puppet back.

697
00:25:03,950 --> 00:25:06,366
Hey, how did that happen?
-That's a good idea.

698
00:25:06,401 --> 00:25:08,679
Gypsy, there's something wrong
with the space-time thingy.

699
00:25:08,714 --> 00:25:11,130
Is there anything we can do?
-Well, okay, Gypsy.

700
00:25:11,164 --> 00:25:12,683
Well, I guess all we can do
is ride it out.

701
00:25:12,718 --> 00:25:14,236
I'm out of here.
-Okay, Gypsy.

702
00:25:14,271 --> 00:25:15,721
I guess all we can do
is ride it out.

703
00:25:15,755 --> 00:25:18,102
I'm --
Wow, it's a weird déjà vu.

704
00:25:18,137 --> 00:25:19,932
-[Laughs]

705
00:25:19,966 --> 00:25:21,243
-Yeah, that's a good idea,
Crow.

706
00:25:21,278 --> 00:25:22,762
You do that.
This is really weird.

707
00:25:22,797 --> 00:25:24,177
We'll be right back.

708
00:25:24,212 --> 00:25:25,489
-Well, I'm just going to play
with my chicken puppet

709
00:25:25,524 --> 00:25:26,766
until this blows over.

710
00:25:26,801 --> 00:25:28,492
I'll see you Mike, Tom.

711
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:30,701
[Whistles]

712
00:25:37,087 --> 00:25:39,572
Hey, anybody seen
my chicken puppet?

713
00:25:40,711 --> 00:25:45,578
♪♪

714
00:25:46,614 --> 00:25:49,202
-Sorghum,
nature's rich bounty,

715
00:25:49,237 --> 00:25:50,859
helping the war effort.

716
00:25:50,894 --> 00:25:53,034
-Still lagging behind,
Crow, huh?

717
00:25:53,068 --> 00:25:54,483
-Shut up.

718
00:25:54,518 --> 00:25:58,246
You know, a scare me would
really help things out here.

719
00:25:58,280 --> 00:25:59,730
-Scare me.

720
00:25:59,765 --> 00:26:02,837
-It's a Sealy Posturepedic
corn field.

721
00:26:02,871 --> 00:26:05,494
-I thought those
Heaven's Gate people

722
00:26:05,529 --> 00:26:07,082
were supposed to meet us here.

723
00:26:07,117 --> 00:26:10,361
♪♪

724
00:26:10,396 --> 00:26:14,331
We have to chop the salads
and then get to the invasion.

725
00:26:14,365 --> 00:26:17,092
-Today's lotto numbers
are 7...

726
00:26:17,127 --> 00:26:18,404
-Careful now.

727
00:26:18,438 --> 00:26:21,062
This microwave searchwill help us locate that prince.

728
00:26:21,096 --> 00:26:22,063
-Mm-hmm.

729
00:26:22,097 --> 00:26:25,722
-We'll find him,
that miserable scum.

730
00:26:25,756 --> 00:26:27,068
-He stole my cup.

731
00:26:27,102 --> 00:26:29,139
-He must be around here
someplace, I'm sure,

732
00:26:29,173 --> 00:26:31,451
and when I find him,
I'm going to kill him myself.

733
00:26:31,486 --> 00:26:33,730
-I was actually signed up
to do that, sir.

734
00:26:33,764 --> 00:26:35,317
-Oh, here he is.

735
00:26:37,147 --> 00:26:39,736
-Location 4 1/2 miles
northwest of here,

736
00:26:39,770 --> 00:26:44,464
Sensitivity's 7.2,
inside a concrete building.

737
00:26:44,499 --> 00:26:46,466
Strong iron reaction.

738
00:26:46,501 --> 00:26:47,744
-Can I move this thing?
Thanks.

739
00:26:47,778 --> 00:26:51,402
-Hm, that puts him
near Macken's laboratory.

740
00:26:51,437 --> 00:26:54,267
Hey, see if you can get it
on the telemonitor.

741
00:26:54,302 --> 00:26:55,303
-Yes, sir.

742
00:26:55,337 --> 00:26:57,892
-[Humming]

743
00:26:57,926 --> 00:27:00,411
-Luxury retirement compounds.

744
00:27:03,069 --> 00:27:06,417
-Right over there, sir.
-Mm-hmm.

745
00:27:06,452 --> 00:27:08,212
-Well, I'm back from break.
Anything shaking?

746
00:27:08,247 --> 00:27:11,008
-All right.
Let's go get him.

747
00:27:11,043 --> 00:27:12,665
Break out the underground tank.

748
00:27:12,700 --> 00:27:15,979
-And they underpants
for a change.

749
00:27:16,013 --> 00:27:17,670
-Attention below there.

750
00:27:17,705 --> 00:27:20,121
Prepare the underground tank.

751
00:27:20,155 --> 00:27:25,264
Coordinate 602 and point 5,
4 1/2 miles northwest of here.

752
00:27:25,298 --> 00:27:26,990
-What gets in
to some civilizations?

753
00:27:27,024 --> 00:27:28,301
-Don't know.

754
00:27:28,336 --> 00:27:30,096
-Pretty small cubicles.

755
00:27:30,131 --> 00:27:33,099
-I've been watching
all morning, but it's no use.

756
00:27:33,134 --> 00:27:34,100
-Why not?

757
00:27:34,135 --> 00:27:35,239
-I think he only comes
around at night.

758
00:27:35,274 --> 00:27:36,689
-Why?
-He's evil,

759
00:27:36,724 --> 00:27:38,829
and evil people
always come around at night?

760
00:27:38,864 --> 00:27:41,383
-Nobody's watching, they even
come in the daytime.

761
00:27:41,418 --> 00:27:42,730
-Although when evil people
are mating,

762
00:27:42,764 --> 00:27:44,904
they will appear
at dawn sometimes.

763
00:27:44,939 --> 00:27:49,633
♪♪

764
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:51,739
-♪ Japan

765
00:27:51,773 --> 00:27:55,294
♪♪

766
00:27:55,328 --> 00:27:56,433
-♪ I'm Hardrock

767
00:27:56,467 --> 00:27:57,779
-♪ I'm Coco 
-♪ I'm Joe

768
00:27:57,814 --> 00:27:59,919
-Hey, look,
there's some funny people.

769
00:27:59,954 --> 00:28:01,645
They're crawling out of a hole.

770
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,681
-Really? Give me that.

771
00:28:02,715 --> 00:28:05,338
-Edna, come look.

772
00:28:05,373 --> 00:28:06,374
-Do we all have to go?

773
00:28:06,408 --> 00:28:09,032
What are we,
a bunch of women or...

774
00:28:09,066 --> 00:28:10,861
-Hey, that looks like
that spaceman.

775
00:28:10,896 --> 00:28:12,104
Remember the other night?

776
00:28:12,138 --> 00:28:13,553
-You're right.
We'll go see.

777
00:28:13,588 --> 00:28:14,554
Come on.

778
00:28:14,589 --> 00:28:16,039
-I have a trial at 3:00.
Let's go.

779
00:28:16,073 --> 00:28:17,696
-Take these, will you?

780
00:28:17,730 --> 00:28:19,249
-Wait.
Where are you going now?

781
00:28:19,283 --> 00:28:20,629
-We're going to spy
on those spacemen.

782
00:28:20,664 --> 00:28:21,838
They're in the old factory.

783
00:28:21,872 --> 00:28:23,218
-What?

784
00:28:23,253 --> 00:28:27,740
♪♪

785
00:28:27,775 --> 00:28:30,743
-We've filled our pants, sir.

786
00:28:30,778 --> 00:28:33,366
-Ready and mince,

787
00:28:33,401 --> 00:28:35,714
mince, mince, mince,
mince, mince, mince,

788
00:28:35,748 --> 00:28:40,097
mince, mince, mince, mince,
mince, mince, mince, mince.

789
00:28:40,132 --> 00:28:41,512
Mince, mince.

790
00:28:41,547 --> 00:28:43,894
-This isn't where we parked.
Oh, yeah, up a level, come on.

791
00:28:43,929 --> 00:28:45,309
♪♪

792
00:28:45,344 --> 00:28:47,311
-The Gabe Kaplan brigade.

793
00:28:47,346 --> 00:28:50,038
♪♪

794
00:28:50,073 --> 00:28:52,144
-A-ha, and now the real reason
we came here,

795
00:28:52,178 --> 00:28:53,421
refurbishing old buildings

796
00:28:53,455 --> 00:28:55,181
and selling them
as affordable condominiums.

797
00:28:55,216 --> 00:28:56,286
Hmm?
-Ah.

798
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:57,459
-Ha-ha.
-Mm-hmm.

799
00:28:57,494 --> 00:28:59,668
♪♪

800
00:28:59,703 --> 00:29:01,187
-They had cats, sir.

801
00:29:01,222 --> 00:29:04,570
-[Laughing]

802
00:29:04,604 --> 00:29:06,399
-Raceway Park!

803
00:29:06,434 --> 00:29:07,469
-You came.

804
00:29:07,504 --> 00:29:09,748
I've been expecting you.

805
00:29:09,782 --> 00:29:11,680
-I came, yes.

806
00:29:11,715 --> 00:29:12,820
-[Laughs]

807
00:29:12,854 --> 00:29:14,407
-And now I'm going to kill you.

808
00:29:14,442 --> 00:29:15,408
-Ha-ha, oh.

809
00:29:15,443 --> 00:29:17,514
-Just how do you propose
to do that?

810
00:29:17,548 --> 00:29:21,345
Your ray guns will have
no effect on me or my ship.

811
00:29:21,380 --> 00:29:22,622
I've told you that already.

812
00:29:22,657 --> 00:29:25,177
-Hold on, I'm getting
a Dodgers game here.

813
00:29:25,211 --> 00:29:27,075
-You'd better leave this planet
in peace.

814
00:29:27,110 --> 00:29:28,974
I warned you once before.

815
00:29:29,008 --> 00:29:30,009
-Get him!

816
00:29:33,357 --> 00:29:35,497
-Come on, little buddy!

817
00:29:35,981 --> 00:29:37,361
-Where did he go?

818
00:29:37,396 --> 00:29:40,088
-He disappeared.
-No, in here, he must be here.

819
00:29:40,123 --> 00:29:41,918
-He's gone.

820
00:29:41,952 --> 00:29:44,023
-That coward, he ran away.

821
00:29:44,058 --> 00:29:45,162
-Looking for me?

822
00:29:45,197 --> 00:29:46,508
-Uh, yeah, we are. Hi.

823
00:29:46,543 --> 00:29:47,820
-I'm not running away.

824
00:29:47,855 --> 00:29:50,098
No, I want to stay because
I'm going to prevent you

825
00:29:50,133 --> 00:29:51,824
from getting
Dr. Macken's formula.

826
00:29:51,859 --> 00:29:52,825
-Kill him!

827
00:29:52,860 --> 00:29:53,861
-Would you guys just listen?

828
00:29:53,895 --> 00:29:55,966
Your guns don't work!

829
00:29:56,001 --> 00:29:57,140
-Some of you go that way.

830
00:29:57,174 --> 00:29:58,382
-Don't let him get away.

831
00:29:58,417 --> 00:29:59,694
-Aah!

832
00:29:59,728 --> 00:30:01,489
-Bring the laser cannon.

833
00:30:01,523 --> 00:30:02,697
-The Prince is there.

834
00:30:02,731 --> 00:30:04,906
-Yeah, he must be fighting
with that Phantom.

835
00:30:07,253 --> 00:30:10,118
-Somebody left a perfectly good
refrigerator over there.

836
00:30:10,153 --> 00:30:13,052
[Laughs]

837
00:30:13,087 --> 00:30:15,572
-Here is the laser cannon, sir.
-Good.

838
00:30:15,606 --> 00:30:17,436
-We can't find him, sir.

839
00:30:17,470 --> 00:30:19,887
-Listen, show yourself,

840
00:30:19,921 --> 00:30:21,889
otherwise we're going
to kill some...dren!

841
00:30:21,923 --> 00:30:23,338
-Kill some diffrin?
-Duffrin?

842
00:30:23,373 --> 00:30:25,547
-I hear you.
Come in here.

843
00:30:25,582 --> 00:30:27,480
I'm waiting for you.

844
00:30:27,515 --> 00:30:28,999
Leave the children alone.

845
00:30:29,034 --> 00:30:31,070
-You hear that, Jerry Seinfeld?

846
00:30:31,105 --> 00:30:34,073
-You cannot harm them anyway
as long as I am here.

847
00:30:34,108 --> 00:30:36,420
-Do You need a ladder?

848
00:30:36,455 --> 00:30:39,009
-I've got you now, you scum.

849
00:30:39,044 --> 00:30:41,115
-Scum, where'd that come from?

850
00:30:42,461 --> 00:30:44,049
-This is the end for you.

851
00:30:44,083 --> 00:30:45,464
-Ya jerk!

852
00:30:45,498 --> 00:30:49,882
-You'll be a horrible example
for anyone who opposes me.

853
00:30:49,917 --> 00:30:51,125
-A really horrible example

854
00:30:51,159 --> 00:30:53,921
because no one else
will ever be scared of him.

855
00:30:56,820 --> 00:30:57,994
-[Laughs]

856
00:30:58,028 --> 00:31:01,100
I told you, your weapons
have no effect on me.

857
00:31:01,135 --> 00:31:02,343
-It is my considered advice

858
00:31:02,377 --> 00:31:04,310
that you discontinue your use
of said weapon!

859
00:31:04,345 --> 00:31:05,484
Ha-ha!

860
00:31:05,518 --> 00:31:06,795
-Aah! Aah! Aah!

861
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:08,521
-See, you are scum!

862
00:31:08,556 --> 00:31:10,075
-Now, I'll wrangle you!

863
00:31:10,109 --> 00:31:11,973
-I'll throw my doll at you!

864
00:31:13,595 --> 00:31:14,838
-Let's go!

865
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:16,771
♪♪

866
00:31:16,805 --> 00:31:18,117
-Whoo.

867
00:31:18,152 --> 00:31:19,291
-Grab the children, grab them!

868
00:31:19,325 --> 00:31:20,913
-Hinnywee away!

869
00:31:20,948 --> 00:31:23,882
-Hey, wait, you go that way.

870
00:31:24,192 --> 00:31:25,469
-Help!
-Help!

871
00:31:25,504 --> 00:31:26,919
-There they are!
Let's grab them!

872
00:31:26,954 --> 00:31:28,956
-You know, this is where
your cram school experience

873
00:31:28,990 --> 00:31:30,474
really comes in handy.

874
00:31:30,509 --> 00:31:32,131
[Both shouting]

875
00:31:32,166 --> 00:31:33,822
-We have to get back
to boot-blacking.

876
00:31:33,857 --> 00:31:36,308
We like it very much.

877
00:31:36,342 --> 00:31:38,137
-Prince, don't let him take me.
-Prince, hide me, please!

878
00:31:38,172 --> 00:31:39,552
-Empirical data suggests

879
00:31:39,587 --> 00:31:41,140
the accuracy
of my earlier contention

880
00:31:41,175 --> 00:31:43,142
that your weapons against me
are without merit!

881
00:31:43,177 --> 00:31:44,247
Ha-ha!

882
00:31:44,281 --> 00:31:45,904
♪♪

883
00:31:45,938 --> 00:31:47,284
-Ooh, ouchie, ouchie,
ouchie, ouchie, ooh!

884
00:31:47,319 --> 00:31:48,320
-Ow!
-Ooh!

885
00:31:48,354 --> 00:31:49,424
-You know how to shoot, Prince.

886
00:31:49,459 --> 00:31:51,219
You're a good shot!

887
00:31:51,254 --> 00:31:52,358
-Hmm?

888
00:31:54,188 --> 00:31:55,603
Oof, my lumbar.

889
00:31:55,637 --> 00:31:56,707
-Oh!

890
00:31:56,742 --> 00:31:57,846
-Come here, you little --

891
00:31:57,881 --> 00:31:59,400
-Help, help, Prince,
help me, help!

892
00:31:59,434 --> 00:32:01,333
-And the tension is thwarted.

893
00:32:01,367 --> 00:32:02,575
-Hey, Prince!

894
00:32:02,610 --> 00:32:04,646
-Please, call me the Artist.

895
00:32:05,993 --> 00:32:07,511
-Did you get hurt?
Are you both all right?

896
00:32:07,546 --> 00:32:09,272
-Yes, Prince.
-Yes, Prince.

897
00:32:09,306 --> 00:32:11,964
-Oh, boy, you beat up
that Phantom pretty good.

898
00:32:11,999 --> 00:32:14,622
-Yes, don't want to
kill him, though.

899
00:32:14,656 --> 00:32:16,796
Listen, the police are coming.
We'd better go now.

900
00:32:16,831 --> 00:32:17,797
-Right.

901
00:32:17,832 --> 00:32:19,868
[Sirens wailing]

902
00:32:19,903 --> 00:32:22,388
-It was so chilly.
I brought my shawl.

903
00:32:22,423 --> 00:32:24,218
-Johnnie, listen to me.

904
00:32:24,252 --> 00:32:25,633
I want to give you something.

905
00:32:25,667 --> 00:32:27,255
Keep it with you always.

906
00:32:27,290 --> 00:32:30,638
If you ever need me again,
just turn the dial, understand?

907
00:32:30,672 --> 00:32:32,847
-I'll turn the dial.
-If you need me.

908
00:32:32,881 --> 00:32:35,505
-You won't tell anybody
about this, agreed?

909
00:32:35,539 --> 00:32:36,368
-Yes.

910
00:32:36,402 --> 00:32:38,128
-All right.
Goodbye now.

911
00:32:38,163 --> 00:32:40,613
-Who are we going
to tell first?

912
00:32:40,648 --> 00:32:41,787
-Hey, there's the commissioner.

913
00:32:41,821 --> 00:32:43,927
-Pete Rozelle?

914
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:45,687
[Rhythmic tapping]

915
00:32:45,722 --> 00:32:48,035
Wow, Tap Dogs.

916
00:32:48,069 --> 00:32:49,968
-Look, there's the kid.
Hey, Mickey!

917
00:32:50,002 --> 00:32:51,728
-Commissioner!
-Commissioner!

918
00:32:51,762 --> 00:32:53,005
-Well, children,
what's going on?

919
00:32:53,040 --> 00:32:54,282
-The Prince of Space
and Phantom,

920
00:32:54,317 --> 00:32:55,318
they were fighting.

921
00:32:55,352 --> 00:32:56,836
Phantom got beat up
and ran away.

922
00:32:56,871 --> 00:32:58,666
-What did you say,
the Prince of Space?

923
00:32:58,700 --> 00:33:00,323
-The one who wears
the flying saucer.

924
00:33:00,357 --> 00:33:01,634
-Yeah.
-The one you saw last night?

925
00:33:01,669 --> 00:33:02,808
-Yeah, that's right.

926
00:33:02,842 --> 00:33:03,878
-And he was here today?
-Yeah.

927
00:33:03,912 --> 00:33:05,224
Right, Johnnie?
-Mm-hmm.

928
00:33:05,259 --> 00:33:06,432
-Good job not telling, kids.

929
00:33:06,467 --> 00:33:07,606
-We're telling the truth.

930
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,470
He even spoke with us.
You know what he said?

931
00:33:09,504 --> 00:33:12,059
-Yeah, he said the spacemen
came here to Earth

932
00:33:12,093 --> 00:33:14,337
to steal
Dr. Macken's new rocket fuel.

933
00:33:14,371 --> 00:33:16,201
-Yeah, the big goomba
is going to take the fuel!

934
00:33:16,235 --> 00:33:18,410
-Commissioner, look at this!

935
00:33:18,444 --> 00:33:20,653
-Terry got my gun dirty.

936
00:33:20,688 --> 00:33:22,621
-Oh, one of those spacemen
was using that.

937
00:33:22,655 --> 00:33:23,967
-One of those spacemen?
-Chief.

938
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:25,796
-One of those spacemen.
-The building is empty.

939
00:33:25,831 --> 00:33:27,902
-Ah, they all got away, huh?

940
00:33:27,936 --> 00:33:29,041
Come on. Your father
is worried about you.

941
00:33:29,076 --> 00:33:30,284
-All right.
-Take over.

942
00:33:30,318 --> 00:33:31,733
-All right. Whatever.

943
00:33:31,768 --> 00:33:34,667
-Wow, it's a really
modern Lutheran church.

944
00:33:34,702 --> 00:33:36,462
♪♪

945
00:33:36,497 --> 00:33:39,672
-We're going to pop in here
for some sushi burritos.

946
00:33:40,225 --> 00:33:41,743
-Dr. Sangamon?

947
00:33:41,778 --> 00:33:43,952
-What is it, boys?

948
00:33:43,987 --> 00:33:46,265
-Please, sir, are you going
to go ahead with the test?

949
00:33:46,300 --> 00:33:48,578
-Of course we are.
-Everything is ready, Doctor.

950
00:33:48,612 --> 00:33:49,958
-Good.

951
00:33:49,993 --> 00:33:51,408
-You kids want to swab out
the particle accelerator?

952
00:33:51,443 --> 00:33:55,757
-Oh, listen, boys, I think
you'd be better off at home.

953
00:33:55,792 --> 00:33:57,069
There's no danger, of course,

954
00:33:57,104 --> 00:33:58,864
but we don't want to take
any chances, right?

955
00:33:58,898 --> 00:34:00,279
-They're kids.

956
00:34:00,314 --> 00:34:01,591
-If this Phantom shows up,

957
00:34:01,625 --> 00:34:03,282
these soldiers aren't
going to be much good.

958
00:34:03,317 --> 00:34:05,871
-Yeah, I wish Prince of Space
was here with us.

959
00:34:05,905 --> 00:34:07,252
-Did you bring the dial
with you?

960
00:34:07,286 --> 00:34:08,356
-Why, sure.

961
00:34:08,391 --> 00:34:09,564
-Why don't we call him
with it, then?

962
00:34:09,599 --> 00:34:10,945
We're not in any trouble,
really,

963
00:34:10,979 --> 00:34:12,843
but we don't want
to take any chances.

964
00:34:12,878 --> 00:34:14,293
-What the hell happened
to my pants?

965
00:34:14,328 --> 00:34:15,743
-What the --

966
00:34:15,777 --> 00:34:17,538
-I'm going to tell him
it was your idea.

967
00:34:17,572 --> 00:34:18,711
-Mm-hmm.

968
00:34:18,746 --> 00:34:20,299
-So if we get busted,
it's your ass!

969
00:34:20,334 --> 00:34:21,783
-Mm-hmm.

970
00:34:21,818 --> 00:34:23,130
-Aah! Aah!

971
00:34:23,164 --> 00:34:25,339
-What a handsome woman.

972
00:34:25,373 --> 00:34:26,409
Oh.

973
00:34:26,443 --> 00:34:27,996
-Laurence, what was that noise?

974
00:34:28,031 --> 00:34:30,206
-Did you hear a noise?
-Mm-hmm.

975
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:32,760
-I only hear the turbines.
-I see.

976
00:34:34,106 --> 00:34:36,419
-Look, it's him!
-The Phantom!

977
00:34:36,453 --> 00:34:38,214
-The little troublemakers, huh?
-When chickens attack.

978
00:34:38,248 --> 00:34:39,284
-We'll take care of you.
All right?

979
00:34:39,318 --> 00:34:41,113
-Help!
-Help, help!

980
00:34:41,148 --> 00:34:46,084
♪♪

981
00:34:46,981 --> 00:34:48,741
-Ah!
-Goodbye.

982
00:34:48,776 --> 00:34:50,157
-I'm retiring and moving
to Florida.

983
00:34:50,191 --> 00:34:52,711
-Well, this is
a great day for us.

984
00:34:52,745 --> 00:34:54,747
-Jimmy Osmond, whoa!

985
00:34:54,782 --> 00:34:57,129
♪♪

986
00:34:57,164 --> 00:34:59,856
-The day is less great now.

987
00:34:59,890 --> 00:35:01,133
-Oh!

988
00:35:01,168 --> 00:35:02,548
[Indistinct shouting]

989
00:35:02,583 --> 00:35:04,343
-For some reason,
it doesn't work on hats.

990
00:35:04,378 --> 00:35:05,448
-Who are you?
What do you want?

991
00:35:05,482 --> 00:35:08,244
-You know what I want:
your rocket fuel.

992
00:35:08,278 --> 00:35:10,625
Those soldiers who werestanding there are good examples

993
00:35:10,660 --> 00:35:12,800
of what my ray guns can do,
Professor,

994
00:35:12,834 --> 00:35:13,939
so don't
try my patience.

995
00:35:13,973 --> 00:35:16,148
-But do try my homemade
griddle cakes.

996
00:35:16,183 --> 00:35:17,805
-Well, are you going to talk?

997
00:35:17,839 --> 00:35:20,221
Or do you want me to start
with the children?

998
00:35:20,256 --> 00:35:23,397
-There's a safe over here.
-Get moving.

999
00:35:23,431 --> 00:35:24,570
-I thought you said

1000
00:35:24,605 --> 00:35:26,365
you were going to start
with the children!

1001
00:35:27,228 --> 00:35:29,299
-Mars, put guards on the door.
-Yes, sir.

1002
00:35:29,334 --> 00:35:30,645
-Mars?

1003
00:35:31,543 --> 00:35:32,992
-No!
-Don't give it to him!

1004
00:35:33,027 --> 00:35:34,304
[Muffled shouting]

1005
00:35:34,339 --> 00:35:35,719
-You'd think they'd consider
taking over

1006
00:35:35,754 --> 00:35:37,721
one of the Earth's good nations.

1007
00:35:37,756 --> 00:35:39,965
-Well, what are you
waiting for?

1008
00:35:39,999 --> 00:35:41,518
I want that safe opened!

1009
00:35:41,553 --> 00:35:42,864
-Oh, sorry,
I'm a little out of it.

1010
00:35:42,899 --> 00:35:45,281
I stayed up and watched
"Letterman" last night.

1011
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:50,217
-Please, I start cram school
at 3 a.m.!

1012
00:35:50,251 --> 00:35:53,220
♪♪

1013
00:35:53,254 --> 00:35:55,429
-If I could only reach
this dried squid!

1014
00:35:55,463 --> 00:35:58,086
♪♪

1015
00:35:58,121 --> 00:36:01,952
-Oh, a secret armoire.

1016
00:36:01,987 --> 00:36:03,299
-Whoops, my doorknob.

1017
00:36:03,333 --> 00:36:04,610
♪♪

1018
00:36:04,645 --> 00:36:05,542
-[Laughs]

1019
00:36:05,577 --> 00:36:06,819
-Ha, this is what I want.

1020
00:36:06,854 --> 00:36:08,925
-The abstracted deed
on your lake property!

1021
00:36:08,959 --> 00:36:11,583
-Let him go!
-Come on!

1022
00:36:11,617 --> 00:36:12,791
-Let him go!
-Come here, you!

1023
00:36:12,825 --> 00:36:15,000
-Give me that remote!
-Ah, Ken!

1024
00:36:15,034 --> 00:36:16,657
-Help us, Prince!
-Please help!

1025
00:36:16,691 --> 00:36:18,486
-Allow me to reference
my earlier codicil

1026
00:36:18,521 --> 00:36:20,385
on how your weapons
are ineffective.

1027
00:36:20,419 --> 00:36:23,353
-Enough, there's no use firing.

1028
00:36:23,388 --> 00:36:24,768
Your guns won't work against me.

1029
00:36:24,803 --> 00:36:26,045
-Have I mentioned that?

1030
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:28,496
-And, Phantom, give the bag
back to the doctor.

1031
00:36:28,531 --> 00:36:29,566
-[Grumbles]

1032
00:36:29,601 --> 00:36:30,602
-What a bunch of crap.

1033
00:36:30,636 --> 00:36:31,844
-Take him!

1034
00:36:31,879 --> 00:36:33,018
[All shout]

1035
00:36:33,052 --> 00:36:34,226
-Prince! Prince!
-Oh!

1036
00:36:34,261 --> 00:36:35,986
-They all have knee goiters.

1037
00:36:36,021 --> 00:36:38,023
-Oh!
-Ah!

1038
00:36:38,057 --> 00:36:39,438
-Oh, Prince!

1039
00:36:39,473 --> 00:36:41,371
-You saved us, Prince!
-Stand clear, boys.

1040
00:36:41,406 --> 00:36:43,166
-Move on, Johnnie.
You're going with me.

1041
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:44,754
One move, and he dies!

1042
00:36:44,788 --> 00:36:46,273
-No, let the boy go!

1043
00:36:46,307 --> 00:36:47,791
-Ah!
-Take the formula.

1044
00:36:47,826 --> 00:36:49,137
Let the boy go!

1045
00:36:49,172 --> 00:36:50,484
-So am I your hostage?

1046
00:36:50,518 --> 00:36:52,486
Should I -- Oh.

1047
00:36:52,520 --> 00:36:56,179
[Sirens wail, men shout]

1048
00:36:56,214 --> 00:36:58,526
-Ha-ha, I guess.

1049
00:37:01,149 --> 00:37:03,290
-"Medical Center,"
starring Evel Knievel.

1050
00:37:03,324 --> 00:37:08,260
[Sirens wailing]

1051
00:37:08,295 --> 00:37:10,676
-They was supposed to meet me
here in the saucer.

1052
00:37:12,782 --> 00:37:14,404
-Air Krankor.

1053
00:37:18,788 --> 00:37:21,411
-Oh, Krankor blew up
a potential tackler on the 40,

1054
00:37:21,446 --> 00:37:25,035
and now there's
nothing but daylight.

1055
00:37:25,070 --> 00:37:27,900
-Your invasion is like
a poorly planned bank heist.

1056
00:37:27,935 --> 00:37:30,213
♪♪

1057
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:31,628
-Ooh, you just opened up

1058
00:37:31,663 --> 00:37:33,734
a whole can of jellied
whoop-ass, pal.

1059
00:37:33,768 --> 00:37:35,080
-Ooh!
-Get him!

1060
00:37:35,114 --> 00:37:36,564
-You know, I'll never go buy
a switching station

1061
00:37:36,599 --> 00:37:38,428
without thinking of this scene.

1062
00:37:40,603 --> 00:37:44,227
-Your guns are useless butscare the crap out of me anyway.

1063
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:46,367
-There's trouble
at the Church of the Bomb.

1064
00:37:49,232 --> 00:37:50,613
-Oh!

1065
00:37:50,647 --> 00:37:54,617
-So, you going to let me invade
your planet now, huh, huh?

1066
00:37:54,651 --> 00:37:57,482
-Oh, no, not that!
Don't touch!

1067
00:37:57,516 --> 00:37:59,207
-You can't use the phone!
It doesn't dial out!

1068
00:37:59,242 --> 00:38:01,658
-Don't touch it!

1069
00:38:01,693 --> 00:38:03,177
Help, help!

1070
00:38:03,211 --> 00:38:05,144
-The easily bamboozled
Prince of Space.

1071
00:38:05,179 --> 00:38:06,422
-Go on, stop him!

1072
00:38:07,423 --> 00:38:09,804
-Meanwhile, at a car wash
in Yokohama...

1073
00:38:11,323 --> 00:38:14,464
♪♪

1074
00:38:14,499 --> 00:38:15,845
-All right. It's fine.
It's fine.

1075
00:38:15,879 --> 00:38:17,398
We got fire insurance.

1076
00:38:17,433 --> 00:38:18,917
It's all right.

1077
00:38:18,951 --> 00:38:20,815
-Never even had time
to tell Houston

1078
00:38:20,850 --> 00:38:22,541
that they had a problem.

1079
00:38:22,576 --> 00:38:24,371
Oh, the inanity!

1080
00:38:24,405 --> 00:38:26,131
-Oh, the Japan-ity!

1081
00:38:26,165 --> 00:38:29,755
[Siren wails]

1082
00:38:29,790 --> 00:38:30,894
-Aw, that's a shame.

1083
00:38:30,929 --> 00:38:34,035
-Dr. Macken, Dr. Macken,
how horrible!

1084
00:38:34,070 --> 00:38:35,589
He blew up the ship!

1085
00:38:35,623 --> 00:38:38,177
Look, there they go now.

1086
00:38:38,212 --> 00:38:40,283
-People looking,
very Spielberg-ian.

1087
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:43,390
-Oh, the Prince of Space,
he's going after them!

1088
00:38:45,461 --> 00:38:49,637
-Yes, I am Prince of Space,
and I am going after them.

1089
00:38:49,672 --> 00:38:51,605
-And his companion,
Duke of Puddles.

1090
00:38:51,639 --> 00:38:56,472
[Buzzing]

1091
00:38:56,506 --> 00:38:58,266
-He sent us some cinnamon rolls.

1092
00:38:58,301 --> 00:39:00,786
There's the icing,
and the dough is usually

1093
00:39:00,821 --> 00:39:03,202
under the icing here.

1094
00:39:03,237 --> 00:39:05,204
-Okay, let's see here.

1095
00:39:05,239 --> 00:39:07,206
"Dear Japan, bite me,
love Prince of Space."

1096
00:39:07,241 --> 00:39:08,725
-"I will bring back the formula

1097
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:11,314
after I chase
these invaders home,

1098
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:13,627
signed Prince of Space."

1099
00:39:13,661 --> 00:39:18,045
-"In the meantime, there may be
many more horrible deaths."

1100
00:39:18,079 --> 00:39:20,358
-Um, Tora?

1101
00:39:20,392 --> 00:39:21,738
-Your attention, please,

1102
00:39:21,773 --> 00:39:23,602
your Red Arrow flight 
from San Francisco

1103
00:39:23,637 --> 00:39:25,880
will land at International 
Airport in 15 minutes.

1104
00:39:25,915 --> 00:39:28,952
Please observe the no-smoking sign when it is lit, thank you.

1105
00:39:28,987 --> 00:39:30,506
-Man, what an ugly bunch
of kids.

1106
00:39:30,540 --> 00:39:31,679
They yours?

1107
00:39:31,714 --> 00:39:33,509
-Doctor, I think you
dropped this photograph.

1108
00:39:33,543 --> 00:39:35,649
-Oh, thank you.

1109
00:39:35,683 --> 00:39:37,029
-That's your sister, isn't it?

1110
00:39:37,064 --> 00:39:39,031
She'd never forgive you
if you lost it.

1111
00:39:39,066 --> 00:39:40,895
-Yeah, don't talk
to me anymore.

1112
00:39:40,930 --> 00:39:42,414
All right?

1113
00:39:42,449 --> 00:39:43,829
[Buzzing]

1114
00:39:43,864 --> 00:39:46,349
-A giant roast turkey!

1115
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:47,902
-Do you want the window seat?

1116
00:39:47,937 --> 00:39:53,011
♪♪

1117
00:39:53,045 --> 00:39:54,806
-Hey, that lady
got extra peanuts!

1118
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:56,497
-Yeah, she got
the whole can, too!

1119
00:40:00,536 --> 00:40:02,848
-♪ Tora, Tora, Tora

1120
00:40:02,883 --> 00:40:04,229
♪ Ba-ba-ba-ba-be-boom

1121
00:40:04,263 --> 00:40:05,679
♪ Da-da-da, Tora

1122
00:40:05,713 --> 00:40:07,439
-You want me, sir?

1123
00:40:07,474 --> 00:40:08,923
-Ah, Captain Munakata,
come in, please.

1124
00:40:08,958 --> 00:40:10,649
-I understand you're
stuffed with cheese.

1125
00:40:10,684 --> 00:40:13,031
-I want you to investigate
the disappearance

1126
00:40:13,065 --> 00:40:14,757
of a civilian aircraft.

1127
00:40:14,791 --> 00:40:16,828
You understand?
-Yes, sir.

1128
00:40:16,862 --> 00:40:18,208
-About 10 minutes ago,

1129
00:40:18,243 --> 00:40:20,418
our radio contact
with the plane was interrupted

1130
00:40:20,452 --> 00:40:21,419
and disappeared from our radar.

1131
00:40:21,453 --> 00:40:22,730
-Who's talking?
-I don't know.

1132
00:40:22,765 --> 00:40:24,767
-At the time, it must have been
approaching Point Barrow.

1133
00:40:24,801 --> 00:40:25,975
-Are we hearing voices?

1134
00:40:26,009 --> 00:40:28,011
-Point Barrow?
-We believe so.

1135
00:40:28,046 --> 00:40:29,565
-I'll go immediately.

1136
00:40:29,599 --> 00:40:31,705
-Or Thursday.

1137
00:40:31,739 --> 00:40:35,398
-Munakata, be careful.
-Yes, sir, I will.

1138
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:38,436
-Love you!

1139
00:40:38,470 --> 00:40:40,438
-Baker tower from 
Dog Charlie 22, come in.

1140
00:40:40,472 --> 00:40:41,818
-Woof, over.

1141
00:40:41,853 --> 00:40:43,475
-Baker tower here, go ahead.

1142
00:40:43,510 --> 00:40:46,478
-Altitude 10,000 feet, 
Point Barrow dead ahead,

1143
00:40:46,513 --> 00:40:47,686
nothing in view.

1144
00:40:47,721 --> 00:40:50,655
We'll circle and investigate, 
over.

1145
00:40:50,689 --> 00:40:52,553
-Roger, over and out.

1146
00:40:52,588 --> 00:40:55,176
-I'm a wasp, over. Bzz.

1147
00:41:01,217 --> 00:41:03,357
-Hey, it's Stevie Wonder.

1148
00:41:03,391 --> 00:41:06,671
♪ Isn't she lovely

1149
00:41:06,705 --> 00:41:09,812
♪ Isn't she wonderful

1150
00:41:09,846 --> 00:41:12,504
-Huh?

1151
00:41:12,539 --> 00:41:13,885
-Aah!

1152
00:41:14,644 --> 00:41:17,026
-Baker tower, Baker tower,

1153
00:41:17,060 --> 00:41:18,648
I...I can't move!

1154
00:41:18,683 --> 00:41:21,099
I...

1155
00:41:21,133 --> 00:41:22,756
I can't move!

1156
00:41:22,790 --> 00:41:24,309
-Oh, wait, sorry, I can move.

1157
00:41:24,343 --> 00:41:26,173
I just forgot how for a second.

1158
00:41:26,207 --> 00:41:29,107
-Dog Charlie, Dog Charlie,
what's the matter?

1159
00:41:29,763 --> 00:41:31,696
Hello, Dog Charlie?

1160
00:41:31,730 --> 00:41:33,318
Come on, please,
what's the matter?

1161
00:41:33,352 --> 00:41:34,630
Can you read me?

1162
00:41:34,664 --> 00:41:36,735
-I...I can't move!

1163
00:41:36,770 --> 00:41:38,806
My instruments --

1164
00:41:38,841 --> 00:41:42,085
my instruments
are going haywire!

1165
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:44,467
-My violin, my tuba haywire!
-Ah!

1166
00:41:44,502 --> 00:41:46,227
-What's the matter?

1167
00:41:46,262 --> 00:41:48,091
-Controls are locked!

1168
00:41:48,126 --> 00:41:50,128
-Munakata, what's the matter?

1169
00:41:50,162 --> 00:41:52,026
-This, this is the matter!

1170
00:41:55,202 --> 00:41:56,168
-Aah!

1171
00:41:56,203 --> 00:41:57,687
-The pilot is teething.

1172
00:42:00,587 --> 00:42:03,728
-Black dragon ship,
black dragon!

1173
00:42:03,762 --> 00:42:04,694
-What?

1174
00:42:04,729 --> 00:42:05,695
-What do you mean, "what"?

1175
00:42:05,730 --> 00:42:07,214
-Munakata, what did you say?

1176
00:42:07,248 --> 00:42:08,698
-What?

1177
00:42:08,733 --> 00:42:10,458
-Aah!

1178
00:42:10,493 --> 00:42:12,391
-Aah, I hit my knee
on the dashboard!

1179
00:42:12,426 --> 00:42:15,153
Wow, hurts!

1180
00:42:15,187 --> 00:42:16,464
-There is dog hair
all over the car.

1181
00:42:16,499 --> 00:42:18,190
Why do you think that is, hmm?

1182
00:42:18,225 --> 00:42:20,296
-Oh, good evening,
Professor?

1183
00:42:20,330 --> 00:42:21,711
-Good evening.

1184
00:42:21,746 --> 00:42:23,886
-And then all the notes
that you asked me to to take

1185
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:24,990
at the conference last week.

1186
00:42:25,025 --> 00:42:26,302
-Yes.

1187
00:42:26,336 --> 00:42:27,614
-I'm sure you'll find
everything in order, Doctor.

1188
00:42:27,648 --> 00:42:28,615
-Mm-hmm.
-Oh, if you did it,

1189
00:42:28,649 --> 00:42:29,754
I'm sure I will.

1190
00:42:29,788 --> 00:42:31,031
-Thank you, sir.

1191
00:42:31,065 --> 00:42:32,688
-Hey, Dad, Dad, wait.

1192
00:42:32,722 --> 00:42:33,654
Wait, Dad!

1193
00:42:33,689 --> 00:42:34,931
-Secretary of children.

1194
00:42:34,966 --> 00:42:36,657
-Oh, John, did you have
a good day at school, son?

1195
00:42:36,692 --> 00:42:38,417
-Yes, I did.
I wanted to talk to you.

1196
00:42:38,452 --> 00:42:40,488
Where are you going?
-To the Defense Ministry.

1197
00:42:40,523 --> 00:42:41,731
-Will you be back soon?

1198
00:42:41,766 --> 00:42:42,836
-No, because I loathe you.

1199
00:42:42,870 --> 00:42:44,734
-Not before your bedtime,
I'm afraid.

1200
00:42:44,769 --> 00:42:46,771
-Ah, gee, Dad,

1201
00:42:46,805 --> 00:42:50,429
I want to talk to you aboutthese invaders from outer space.

1202
00:42:50,464 --> 00:42:52,362
-He's putting a cigarette
out on him.

1203
00:42:52,397 --> 00:42:53,950
-Ow.

1204
00:42:53,985 --> 00:42:55,642
-Well, let's talk about it
tomorrow morning

1205
00:42:55,676 --> 00:42:58,058
at breakfast, huh?

1206
00:42:58,092 --> 00:42:59,853
-Um, how come
you're so old, Dad?

1207
00:42:59,887 --> 00:43:02,959
Did you have me when you were,
like, 60 or something?

1208
00:43:02,994 --> 00:43:04,961
-Well, I'm afraid I'm a bit
late for this conference.

1209
00:43:04,996 --> 00:43:06,687
Major Merke will be worried.

1210
00:43:06,722 --> 00:43:08,033
Will you call him
and tell him I'm on my way?

1211
00:43:08,068 --> 00:43:09,966
-Most certainly,
goodbye, Doctor.

1212
00:43:10,001 --> 00:43:13,245
-Bye, Dad, and don't
forget our theory.

1213
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:15,834
-Goodbye, people I seem
to share a house with.

1214
00:43:19,148 --> 00:43:20,252
-Goodbye.

1215
00:43:21,012 --> 00:43:23,877
-I'm sorry.
Dr. Macken has not yet arrived.

1216
00:43:23,911 --> 00:43:26,051
-But, Major, what could
have happened to him?

1217
00:43:26,086 --> 00:43:28,122
-Oh, what?
-It's not like Macken at all

1218
00:43:28,157 --> 00:43:29,952
to be this late
for an appointment.

1219
00:43:29,986 --> 00:43:31,643
-Gentlemen,
I'm quite alarmed about this.

1220
00:43:31,678 --> 00:43:33,093
Dr. Macken may be in trouble.

1221
00:43:33,127 --> 00:43:35,233
In any case,
we can do nothing without him.

1222
00:43:35,267 --> 00:43:38,098
The police may be able
to determine his whereabouts.

1223
00:43:38,132 --> 00:43:39,409
Major Merke,
with your permission...

1224
00:43:39,444 --> 00:43:40,548
-Merke?
-...I will attend

1225
00:43:40,583 --> 00:43:41,619
to this matter immediately.

1226
00:43:41,653 --> 00:43:43,655
-Very good, Captain, go ahead.
-Yes.

1227
00:43:43,690 --> 00:43:44,794
-Gentlemen, I suggest

1228
00:43:44,829 --> 00:43:46,347
a 1/2-hour recess
while the captain...

1229
00:43:46,382 --> 00:43:47,659
-Recess!
-Woo-hoo!

1230
00:43:47,694 --> 00:43:49,212
-Recess!
-Yay!

1231
00:43:50,351 --> 00:43:52,250
-Wow, the Earth is so smooth.

1232
00:43:52,284 --> 00:43:54,148
It must have had dermabrasion.

1233
00:43:57,220 --> 00:44:00,361
-Sounds like the Earth
needs new brake pads.

1234
00:44:00,396 --> 00:44:01,708
-See how things are going.

1235
00:44:01,742 --> 00:44:04,262
-Okay, we'll check it out.

1236
00:44:09,232 --> 00:44:14,272
♪♪

1237
00:44:15,135 --> 00:44:17,137
-Yeah, it seems like it,
doesn't it?

1238
00:44:17,171 --> 00:44:18,863
-So you think we're back in syncon the whole time thing?

1239
00:44:18,897 --> 00:44:19,967
-D'oh!

1240
00:44:20,002 --> 00:44:21,003
-I'm sorry, sorry,
just keep...

1241
00:44:21,037 --> 00:44:22,349
-Okay, hey, guys, listen up.
-What?

1242
00:44:22,383 --> 00:44:23,695
-I think I have some answers.

1243
00:44:23,730 --> 00:44:26,594
Apparently the separateuniverse layers are commingling.

1244
00:44:26,629 --> 00:44:28,976
If we don't isolate our position
in space and time,

1245
00:44:29,011 --> 00:44:31,945
limitless potential...
Wait, wait, what, wh -- what?

1246
00:44:31,979 --> 00:44:34,154
-Uh, Mike,
you're a small robot.

1247
00:44:34,188 --> 00:44:35,258
-Yeah.

1248
00:44:35,293 --> 00:44:37,433
-Of course I am.
What do you expect?

1249
00:44:37,467 --> 00:44:39,677
-Well, normally when we're not
in a wormhole and stuff,

1250
00:44:39,711 --> 00:44:41,748
you're a big,
chunky human thing.

1251
00:44:41,782 --> 00:44:43,922
-And I don't mean to offend you
or anything,

1252
00:44:43,957 --> 00:44:46,511
but as you are, I have the urge
to put you back in your cage.

1253
00:44:46,545 --> 00:44:48,686
-Co --
come on, cut it out, now.

1254
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:50,342
I can't speak for your reality.
-Okay.

1255
00:44:50,377 --> 00:44:52,759
-But in mine, we are all robots
serving on this vessel,

1256
00:44:52,793 --> 00:44:54,208
and I'm in command.
-Uh, uh...

1257
00:44:54,243 --> 00:44:55,520
-You have tremendous
respect for me.

1258
00:44:55,554 --> 00:44:56,555
You do.
-Yeah, uh-huh.

1259
00:44:56,590 --> 00:44:57,764
-Now, now, my orders
are as follows --

1260
00:44:57,798 --> 00:44:59,041
I want you to --
-Sorry, Mike,

1261
00:44:59,075 --> 00:45:01,388
I only take orders
from Willie Tyler and Lester.

1262
00:45:01,422 --> 00:45:03,735
-Oh, oh, that's --
that's a -- Stop.

1263
00:45:03,770 --> 00:45:04,874
Now, come on.
Stop it.

1264
00:45:04,909 --> 00:45:06,048
-Okay, I'm sorry.
-No, stop. Now listen up.

1265
00:45:06,082 --> 00:45:07,566
We all want to get back, right?
-Yeah.

1266
00:45:07,601 --> 00:45:08,913
-Okay, okay, listen up.
-Okay. Sorry.

1267
00:45:08,947 --> 00:45:11,363
-If we want to put things
right, you'll do just as I say.

1268
00:45:11,398 --> 00:45:13,227
If we can overdrive
the plasma thrusters

1269
00:45:13,262 --> 00:45:14,573
to create a gravity well

1270
00:45:14,608 --> 00:45:16,783
isolating us
from the other universe layers,

1271
00:45:16,817 --> 00:45:18,474
we untangle
our commingling realm.

1272
00:45:18,508 --> 00:45:20,303
-I think he just looks --
-Hey, cut it --

1273
00:45:20,338 --> 00:45:21,891
-He's so cute!
-Come on. Cut it out!

1274
00:45:21,926 --> 00:45:23,651
You guys, we're going to be
annihilated and stuff!

1275
00:45:23,686 --> 00:45:24,894
-Oh, Mike, I don't care, man.

1276
00:45:24,929 --> 00:45:26,344
It's worth it
to see you like this.

1277
00:45:26,378 --> 00:45:27,345
-No, stop it!

1278
00:45:27,379 --> 00:45:28,967
Dude! We got movies.

1279
00:45:29,002 --> 00:45:30,210
-Get out of here,
get out of here!

1280
00:45:30,244 --> 00:45:32,971
-Don't push. Don't push.
Don't push. Don't push.

1281
00:45:43,810 --> 00:45:46,191
-Come on. Move it, short stuff.
-I'm moving. I'm moving.

1282
00:45:46,226 --> 00:45:47,814
-Move it, shrimp.
-Don't push, I'm fine.

1283
00:45:47,848 --> 00:45:49,436
-Yes.

1284
00:45:49,470 --> 00:45:51,231
-It says,
"Employees must wash hands

1285
00:45:51,265 --> 00:45:53,164
before returning to invasions."

1286
00:45:57,547 --> 00:45:59,411
-A mummified Alf Landon!

1287
00:45:59,446 --> 00:46:00,619
-Ew.

1288
00:46:04,658 --> 00:46:06,004
-Good morning, honey.

1289
00:46:06,039 --> 00:46:09,318
-Professor Macken,
welcome aboard.

1290
00:46:09,352 --> 00:46:11,769
-Who are you?
-Come, come, Professor,

1291
00:46:11,803 --> 00:46:13,771
permit me
to introduce myself.

1292
00:46:13,805 --> 00:46:17,844
They call me Phantom of Krankor,

1293
00:46:17,878 --> 00:46:19,431
but you seem startled,
Professor.

1294
00:46:19,466 --> 00:46:21,295
Sit down. Relax.

1295
00:46:21,330 --> 00:46:24,712
-Hey, Z7, suck it in!

1296
00:46:24,747 --> 00:46:26,335
-Is this a dream?

1297
00:46:26,369 --> 00:46:27,785
Where am I?

1298
00:46:27,819 --> 00:46:29,131
-You want to know
where you are?

1299
00:46:29,165 --> 00:46:30,339
-No, I want to know how --

1300
00:46:30,373 --> 00:46:31,443
Of course I want to know
where I am!

1301
00:46:31,478 --> 00:46:34,170
-You are aboard my flagship,

1302
00:46:34,205 --> 00:46:38,519
halfway between
your world and Krankor.

1303
00:46:38,554 --> 00:46:40,763
-How did you bring me here?

1304
00:46:40,798 --> 00:46:42,247
-For a man
of your intelligence,

1305
00:46:42,282 --> 00:46:44,284
a full explanation
would be necessary.

1306
00:46:44,318 --> 00:46:45,423
-Oh.

1307
00:46:45,457 --> 00:46:47,045
-But we have no time
for that, Professor.

1308
00:46:47,080 --> 00:46:48,150
-Yay.

1309
00:46:48,184 --> 00:46:49,496
-Well, what about my chauffeur?

1310
00:46:49,530 --> 00:46:53,017
-Come now, my dear Professor,
what a silly question.

1311
00:46:53,051 --> 00:46:56,710
Do you expect me to keep track
of your worthless servants?

1312
00:46:56,744 --> 00:46:58,505
We blasted him out
of an air lock,

1313
00:46:58,539 --> 00:47:01,266
so by now he may have
fallen into a star.

1314
00:47:01,301 --> 00:47:05,236
[Laughs]

1315
00:47:05,270 --> 00:47:07,376
-Wow, this guy is nuttier
than a Stuckey's log.

1316
00:47:07,410 --> 00:47:10,793
-Well, I suppose
that you expect me to help you

1317
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:12,105
with your evil plans.

1318
00:47:12,139 --> 00:47:13,727
-Yeah, would you mind?
Thanks.

1319
00:47:13,761 --> 00:47:16,937
-That is precisely why I gave
orders to take you aboard.

1320
00:47:16,972 --> 00:47:20,492
I will show you much here
that only you can appreciate,

1321
00:47:20,527 --> 00:47:21,666
for example,

1322
00:47:21,700 --> 00:47:23,841
how I propose to control
the universe.

1323
00:47:23,875 --> 00:47:24,842
-Yeah.

1324
00:47:24,876 --> 00:47:25,843
-And when you have
seen all this...

1325
00:47:25,877 --> 00:47:27,327
-So cute.

1326
00:47:27,361 --> 00:47:28,707
-...you will realize
how futile it is

1327
00:47:28,742 --> 00:47:30,778
for you or anyone else
to oppose me.

1328
00:47:30,813 --> 00:47:33,436
-Fine, just go light
on the probes.

1329
00:47:34,506 --> 00:47:37,302
-Making no progress at all.

1330
00:47:37,337 --> 00:47:41,168
-It's incredible how accurate
this is at depicting space.

1331
00:47:42,618 --> 00:47:45,310
-♪ Some people call me
the space cowboy ♪

1332
00:47:45,345 --> 00:47:46,622
♪ Yeah

1333
00:47:48,589 --> 00:47:50,212
-Hey, look at that!

1334
00:47:50,246 --> 00:47:52,352
-Oh, oh, I'm sorry.
I got distracted.

1335
00:47:52,386 --> 00:47:54,526
-Ah, oh!

1336
00:47:54,561 --> 00:47:56,045
-Well, up there is
the kids' playroom.

1337
00:47:56,080 --> 00:47:58,496
And we're going to, yeah.

1338
00:47:58,530 --> 00:48:00,153
-Hey, Chief, we got thatflying saucer on the televisers.

1339
00:48:00,187 --> 00:48:01,637
It's coming up fast astern.

1340
00:48:01,671 --> 00:48:02,707
-What?

1341
00:48:02,741 --> 00:48:04,433
-What?

1342
00:48:04,467 --> 00:48:06,055
-Get him back to his quarters
under guard.

1343
00:48:06,090 --> 00:48:07,298
-Right, sir.

1344
00:48:07,332 --> 00:48:08,299
Come on, you.

1345
00:48:08,333 --> 00:48:09,748
-Oh, Speed, oh.

1346
00:48:09,783 --> 00:48:11,543
-Come on, I said!

1347
00:48:11,578 --> 00:48:14,650
-It's "The Instant Miso Soup
Hour," starring...

1348
00:48:14,684 --> 00:48:18,033
[Humming "Pop Goes the Weasel"]

1349
00:48:20,518 --> 00:48:23,348
-Ah, it's him, alright.

1350
00:48:23,383 --> 00:48:26,524
-Saying "it is me" will have
no effect on me, a-ha.

1351
00:48:28,664 --> 00:48:31,805
-It's a flying
rotary nose-hair clipper.

1352
00:48:31,839 --> 00:48:33,013
-I've got him
right where I want him!

1353
00:48:33,048 --> 00:48:35,913
-Somewhere in space.

1354
00:48:35,947 --> 00:48:36,914
-Don't look at my butt.

1355
00:48:36,948 --> 00:48:39,123
-Now he dies.

1356
00:48:39,157 --> 00:48:41,849
-Just want to test some
batteries here first, though.

1357
00:48:41,884 --> 00:48:43,851
[Laser firing]

1358
00:48:43,886 --> 00:48:46,302
-A-ha, and they stay
crunchy in milk, hmm!

1359
00:48:46,337 --> 00:48:48,787
[Laser fire continues]

1360
00:48:48,822 --> 00:48:50,997
-Swing me over there,
trusty string.

1361
00:48:53,482 --> 00:48:55,933
-He's in the Wienermobile.

1362
00:48:57,693 --> 00:48:59,937
-Oh, no, he lost control
of his fried egg!

1363
00:49:03,457 --> 00:49:05,356
-Enough.
-Right, sir.

1364
00:49:05,390 --> 00:49:07,220
-He's finished.
-Look at...Look at that.

1365
00:49:07,254 --> 00:49:08,497
-And the boob thought
he could follow us...

1366
00:49:08,531 --> 00:49:09,601
-Oh, don't.
-No.

1367
00:49:09,636 --> 00:49:11,258
-...through a shower
of meteorites.

1368
00:49:11,293 --> 00:49:13,536
[Laughs]

1369
00:49:13,571 --> 00:49:17,126
-I have to tell Fang
about that, ha!

1370
00:49:19,163 --> 00:49:21,889
-They're landing
on Captain Picard's head.

1371
00:49:23,305 --> 00:49:25,755
-Oh, it's the planet where
sea monkeys come from.

1372
00:49:28,966 --> 00:49:31,485
-Wow, look at that,
look at that!

1373
00:49:31,520 --> 00:49:33,349
-A trip to Mike's subconscious.

1374
00:49:33,384 --> 00:49:35,696
-It's pretty accurate.
I've got to admit.

1375
00:49:35,731 --> 00:49:37,836
-It's a DQ planet.

1376
00:49:40,149 --> 00:49:42,427
-Dress to the right stuff.

1377
00:49:43,877 --> 00:49:46,017
-Chafe, chafe,
chafe, chafe, chafe, chafe...

1378
00:49:46,052 --> 00:49:47,605
-Shall I put Macken
with the others?

1379
00:49:47,639 --> 00:49:49,193
-Of course not.

1380
00:49:49,227 --> 00:49:50,401
Bring him to the great hall.

1381
00:49:50,435 --> 00:49:51,402
-Right, sir.

1382
00:49:51,436 --> 00:49:52,851
-And prepare to return
to Earth.

1383
00:49:52,886 --> 00:49:53,991
-Right, sir.

1384
00:49:54,025 --> 00:49:57,304
-Uh, didn't we just get back
from Earth, sir?

1385
00:49:57,339 --> 00:50:00,169
-Sir, do we have a plan?
Or...

1386
00:50:00,204 --> 00:50:02,102
-So cracked corn
all around then, gentlemen?

1387
00:50:02,137 --> 00:50:03,276
-I have a special job for you.

1388
00:50:03,310 --> 00:50:04,449
-Yes, sir.

1389
00:50:04,484 --> 00:50:05,968
-I want you to find
that Prince of Space.

1390
00:50:06,003 --> 00:50:09,075
-Prince of Space?
-You heard me right.

1391
00:50:09,109 --> 00:50:10,628
He may have possibly
escaped destruction

1392
00:50:10,662 --> 00:50:12,457
when we passed through
that meteorite shower.

1393
00:50:12,492 --> 00:50:13,734
-Prince of Space, sir?

1394
00:50:13,769 --> 00:50:15,702
-I must have positive proof
that he is finished.

1395
00:50:15,736 --> 00:50:16,841
-Prince of Space, then.

1396
00:50:16,875 --> 00:50:18,118
-He may make
some foolish attempt

1397
00:50:18,153 --> 00:50:19,740
to rescue our prisoners

1398
00:50:19,775 --> 00:50:22,053
and disrupt my plans
for the Earth.

1399
00:50:22,088 --> 00:50:23,296
-Uh, sir, no,
I was going to ask you

1400
00:50:23,330 --> 00:50:25,505
if I should bring this
to the lab, don't! Oh.

1401
00:50:25,539 --> 00:50:26,816
-The last we saw of his ship,

1402
00:50:26,851 --> 00:50:28,197
it was falling away
toward Earth.

1403
00:50:28,232 --> 00:50:30,234
He may possibly have been able
to return to his base.

1404
00:50:30,268 --> 00:50:31,442
-Prince of Space?

1405
00:50:31,476 --> 00:50:32,650
-Does he have a base there?
-I don't know.

1406
00:50:32,684 --> 00:50:33,754
-Of course, he must have
a base somewhere.

1407
00:50:33,789 --> 00:50:35,066
-That's right.

1408
00:50:35,101 --> 00:50:37,793
He must have one there,
and I want you to find it.

1409
00:50:37,827 --> 00:50:38,966
-I'll find it.
All right.

1410
00:50:39,001 --> 00:50:40,451
I can promise you that.

1411
00:50:40,485 --> 00:50:43,178
-You'd better take the X-radar
with you to help you find him.

1412
00:50:43,212 --> 00:50:46,871
Isha will give you
the formula for his wavelength.

1413
00:50:46,905 --> 00:50:47,734
You.

1414
00:50:47,768 --> 00:50:48,976
-Bite me.
-Accompany him.

1415
00:50:49,011 --> 00:50:50,047
-Right, sir.

1416
00:50:50,081 --> 00:50:52,014
-Install the X-radar

1417
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:53,636
in one of the ground cars
of the Earthlings

1418
00:50:53,671 --> 00:50:55,742
and comb the city for him.

1419
00:50:55,776 --> 00:50:57,157
-Ah?
-Ah?

1420
00:50:57,192 --> 00:50:58,986
-He's bound to be disguised,
of course,

1421
00:50:59,021 --> 00:51:01,644
perhaps as a civilian,
but if it's properly set up,

1422
00:51:01,679 --> 00:51:03,267
the X-radar
will find him easily.

1423
00:51:03,301 --> 00:51:04,371
-Huh?
-Oh, hmm.

1424
00:51:04,406 --> 00:51:06,718
-And when you find him,
report to me,

1425
00:51:06,753 --> 00:51:09,100
and above all,
keep track of him.

1426
00:51:09,135 --> 00:51:12,241
I prefer to deal
personally with him.

1427
00:51:12,276 --> 00:51:14,795
And if you don't find him,
don't bother to come back.

1428
00:51:14,830 --> 00:51:17,522
-Right, sir,
we go to obey orders.

1429
00:51:17,557 --> 00:51:18,558
-Dismissed.

1430
00:51:18,592 --> 00:51:20,525
-First we have to go
to the bathroom.

1431
00:51:20,560 --> 00:51:23,114
-Professor Macken is waiting
for you in the great hall.

1432
00:51:23,149 --> 00:51:25,220
-Always quarter to 3:00
here at Krankor's place.

1433
00:51:25,254 --> 00:51:28,878
-Good.

1434
00:51:28,913 --> 00:51:31,088
You, bring in the others
and put them up on the stage.

1435
00:51:31,122 --> 00:51:32,296
-Yes, sir.

1436
00:51:32,744 --> 00:51:35,851
-I'm ashamed of my talk show.

1437
00:51:35,885 --> 00:51:39,579
-Great hall designed
by the LEGO corporation.

1438
00:51:39,613 --> 00:51:41,339
-Well, we don't have
as big a turnout

1439
00:51:41,374 --> 00:51:42,685
as we expected tonight,

1440
00:51:42,720 --> 00:51:45,274
so if we could all justmove down to the first few rows.

1441
00:51:45,309 --> 00:51:46,758
-At ease, men.

1442
00:51:46,793 --> 00:51:48,174
-I mean, man.

1443
00:51:48,208 --> 00:51:51,280
-Professor Macken,
I want to bid you welcome

1444
00:51:51,315 --> 00:51:56,147
to the planet of Krankor
and my home.

1445
00:51:56,182 --> 00:51:59,944
You must have seen a lot
from the window of my flagship:

1446
00:51:59,978 --> 00:52:02,567
the castle cut
from the living rock,

1447
00:52:02,602 --> 00:52:04,604
my giant guardian and so forth.

1448
00:52:04,638 --> 00:52:05,777
-Whatnot and what have you.

1449
00:52:05,812 --> 00:52:08,228
-And I have many more wonders
to show you.

1450
00:52:08,263 --> 00:52:09,781
And I have even brought

1451
00:52:09,816 --> 00:52:10,989
some friends of yours

1452
00:52:11,024 --> 00:52:13,337
to share
this experience with you.

1453
00:52:13,371 --> 00:52:16,650
-Can I get more coffee
over here, please?

1454
00:52:16,685 --> 00:52:20,413
-Bookend Mr. Mooneys.

1455
00:52:20,447 --> 00:52:21,966
-All my rowdy friends!

1456
00:52:22,000 --> 00:52:23,001
-Dr. Fletcher!

1457
00:52:23,036 --> 00:52:25,280
-Oh, Macken!

1458
00:52:25,314 --> 00:52:26,557
-I'm scared!

1459
00:52:26,591 --> 00:52:27,834
-Are you all right?

1460
00:52:27,868 --> 00:52:28,973
-Oh, Professor.

1461
00:52:29,007 --> 00:52:32,459
-I forgot to water
your plants, ah.

1462
00:52:32,494 --> 00:52:34,047
-Lucille!

1463
00:52:34,081 --> 00:52:35,152
-It's Dr. Cummings!

1464
00:52:35,186 --> 00:52:37,430
-Yes, and his assistant
Professor Koi.

1465
00:52:37,464 --> 00:52:38,638
-Lucille.

1466
00:52:38,672 --> 00:52:40,536
-Oh, I'm so sorry about this,
Dr. Cummings.

1467
00:52:40,571 --> 00:52:43,401
-And here is Professor Doriex
from the Southern Institute.

1468
00:52:43,436 --> 00:52:45,023
-Lucille.
-Oh.

1469
00:52:45,058 --> 00:52:48,095
♪♪

1470
00:52:48,130 --> 00:52:49,096
-Mrs. Carmichael.

1471
00:52:49,131 --> 00:52:50,443
-If you don't mind, gentlemen,

1472
00:52:50,477 --> 00:52:52,341
we have much to discuss.

1473
00:52:52,376 --> 00:52:53,618
-Oh.

1474
00:52:53,653 --> 00:52:55,206
-Please sit down.

1475
00:52:55,241 --> 00:52:56,207
-Please.

1476
00:52:56,242 --> 00:52:59,279
No, really, please,
sit down.

1477
00:52:59,314 --> 00:53:00,694
There.

1478
00:53:00,729 --> 00:53:03,145
-So they're alien except for
their Chippendale furniture.

1479
00:53:03,180 --> 00:53:05,112
-Sorry I'm late.
Cat threw up this morning.

1480
00:53:05,147 --> 00:53:06,217
Hi.

1481
00:53:06,252 --> 00:53:07,391
-Very good.

1482
00:53:07,425 --> 00:53:08,426
-You sit well.

1483
00:53:08,461 --> 00:53:10,187
-Everyone I need seems
to be here.

1484
00:53:10,221 --> 00:53:13,362
I appreciate your coming,
gentlemen.

1485
00:53:13,397 --> 00:53:15,778
I am honored to find myself
in the company

1486
00:53:15,813 --> 00:53:18,885
of five of the most
advanced minds of Earth.

1487
00:53:18,919 --> 00:53:20,749
Please make yourselves
comfortable...

1488
00:53:20,783 --> 00:53:21,819
-Until they arrive.

1489
00:53:21,853 --> 00:53:23,752
-...while I explain my plans,

1490
00:53:23,786 --> 00:53:27,342
plans in which you gentlemen
play a very important part.

1491
00:53:27,376 --> 00:53:28,964
[Laughs]

1492
00:53:28,998 --> 00:53:30,207
-I have to leave early.

1493
00:53:30,241 --> 00:53:32,416
-Wait, you can't!
This is impossible!

1494
00:53:32,450 --> 00:53:37,179
-Be silent,
I'm dictator of Krankor.

1495
00:53:37,214 --> 00:53:41,045
I assure you
that the word impossible

1496
00:53:41,079 --> 00:53:43,772
is a word, which for me,
does not exist.

1497
00:53:43,806 --> 00:53:44,980
-Although I just said it.

1498
00:53:45,014 --> 00:53:47,707
-Now first of all,
Professor Macken,

1499
00:53:47,741 --> 00:53:50,192
I've arranged
an interesting show for you.

1500
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:55,128
I trust that you will find it
quite instructive, go ahead.

1501
00:53:55,162 --> 00:53:59,305
-♪ Do-do-do,
Bum-bum, ba-da dum-dum ♪

1502
00:54:00,029 --> 00:54:01,721
-Lean forward.

1503
00:54:05,103 --> 00:54:07,968
-Why, that --
why, that's my house!

1504
00:54:08,003 --> 00:54:08,831
-Oh!

1505
00:54:08,866 --> 00:54:09,936
-So it is.

1506
00:54:09,970 --> 00:54:12,041
You are quite right,
Professor Macken,

1507
00:54:12,076 --> 00:54:13,042
your house.

1508
00:54:13,077 --> 00:54:14,251
-You win this round.

1509
00:54:14,285 --> 00:54:17,150
-And it's half a million
Earth miles from here.

1510
00:54:17,184 --> 00:54:18,979
-But it's on the bus line.

1511
00:54:21,188 --> 00:54:23,190
-Oh, Johnnie!

1512
00:54:23,225 --> 00:54:26,504
-They slammed the iron gate on
me at cram school again today!

1513
00:54:26,539 --> 00:54:30,336
[Classical music plays]

1514
00:54:30,370 --> 00:54:33,960
-Samuel Barber's "Adagio
for Young Japanese Children."

1515
00:54:33,994 --> 00:54:36,307
[Music stops]

1516
00:54:36,342 --> 00:54:37,998
And it's gone.

1517
00:54:38,033 --> 00:54:40,311
-Well, I'm sure this little
scene is leading somewhere,

1518
00:54:40,346 --> 00:54:42,037
if you'll all be patient.

1519
00:54:42,071 --> 00:54:43,694
-Now watch as we turn
the lawn sprinklers

1520
00:54:43,728 --> 00:54:46,455
on our little Johnnie.

1521
00:54:46,490 --> 00:54:48,837
-There's the Japanese
Suzanne Pleshette.

1522
00:54:54,049 --> 00:54:58,260
-Geez, my life
is really boring!

1523
00:54:59,296 --> 00:55:01,056
-Well, gentlemen...
-Ah!

1524
00:55:01,090 --> 00:55:02,091
-...what do you think of that?
-What?

1525
00:55:02,126 --> 00:55:03,541
Oh, wait, they just
got better, yeah.

1526
00:55:03,576 --> 00:55:05,750
-As you saw, nothing you do
on Earth can be hidden from me.

1527
00:55:05,785 --> 00:55:07,476
I've watched all of your secretsfrom here.

1528
00:55:07,511 --> 00:55:09,996
You see, I've been watching you
for a long time now.

1529
00:55:10,030 --> 00:55:11,342
-He knows about the porn.

1530
00:55:11,377 --> 00:55:13,965
-And I knew right where
to find you when I wanted to.

1531
00:55:14,000 --> 00:55:15,622
-So you know about my rash?

1532
00:55:15,657 --> 00:55:17,244
-That's an impressive toy,
but first of all,

1533
00:55:17,279 --> 00:55:18,798
I demand to know
why you brought us here!

1534
00:55:18,832 --> 00:55:21,525
-Grab some bench, lumpy.
-You demand nothing.

1535
00:55:21,559 --> 00:55:23,354
You will merely obey
my instructions.

1536
00:55:23,389 --> 00:55:25,011
-Ah.
-Take your place

1537
00:55:25,045 --> 00:55:26,702
and remain silent

1538
00:55:26,737 --> 00:55:29,636
while I explain
why you were brought here.

1539
00:55:29,671 --> 00:55:30,534
-Ah.

1540
00:55:30,568 --> 00:55:32,018
-You five men are among

1541
00:55:32,052 --> 00:55:34,123
the top scientists of Earth.

1542
00:55:34,158 --> 00:55:36,367
Your governments
respect your opinions.

1543
00:55:36,402 --> 00:55:38,852
Thus, you men are well-equipped
to evaluate my power.

1544
00:55:38,887 --> 00:55:40,302
-One, two, uh-huh.

1545
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:43,098
-You know I can exterminate
the world any time I want to.

1546
00:55:43,132 --> 00:55:44,306
-Quack.

1547
00:55:44,341 --> 00:55:45,618
-I want you to explain this
to your people,

1548
00:55:45,652 --> 00:55:47,965
impress upon them how useless
it would be to oppose me.

1549
00:55:47,999 --> 00:55:49,138
-Quack.

1550
00:55:49,173 --> 00:55:50,761
-You will tell them
I demand their surrender.

1551
00:55:50,795 --> 00:55:52,245
You...

1552
00:55:52,279 --> 00:55:53,211
-Bite me!

1553
00:55:53,246 --> 00:55:54,937
-...You,
each and every one of you.

1554
00:55:54,972 --> 00:55:56,249
-Bite me!
-No, I won't!

1555
00:55:56,283 --> 00:55:57,388
It's out of the question.

1556
00:55:57,423 --> 00:55:58,803
I won't!

1557
00:55:58,838 --> 00:56:00,218
I will never betray my people!

1558
00:56:00,253 --> 00:56:03,221
-I refuse, categorically.
-I will never be your tool!

1559
00:56:03,256 --> 00:56:05,396
-None of us will!
-Agreed?

1560
00:56:05,431 --> 00:56:07,053
-Of course we agree.

1561
00:56:07,087 --> 00:56:08,123
-I'll do it.

1562
00:56:08,157 --> 00:56:10,470
-Apparently you gentlemen
are upset.

1563
00:56:10,505 --> 00:56:12,990
I will give you a chance
to think it over calmly.

1564
00:56:13,024 --> 00:56:14,509
After all,
you are men of science.

1565
00:56:14,543 --> 00:56:15,751
-Eh.

1566
00:56:15,786 --> 00:56:17,684
-We are leaving to attack
your world in 12 hours.

1567
00:56:17,719 --> 00:56:18,961
-What are they going to do?

1568
00:56:18,996 --> 00:56:20,963
-With your cooperation
or without it,

1569
00:56:20,998 --> 00:56:22,758
I am going to attack.

1570
00:56:22,793 --> 00:56:25,692
I shall destroy one of your
major cities first.

1571
00:56:25,727 --> 00:56:28,005
Afterward, I'm sure
you will cooperate.

1572
00:56:28,039 --> 00:56:30,007
[Laughs]

1573
00:56:30,041 --> 00:56:31,353
-His heart is really
not in it, is it?

1574
00:56:31,388 --> 00:56:32,734
-No.
-Ah.

1575
00:56:32,768 --> 00:56:33,942
-It's a "Young Ones" ship.

1576
00:56:33,976 --> 00:56:37,773
[Buzzing]

1577
00:56:37,808 --> 00:56:39,361
-It's kind of hard to go
into warp drive

1578
00:56:39,396 --> 00:56:41,052
when you're burning so much oil.

1579
00:56:41,087 --> 00:56:42,399
-Professor, may I?

1580
00:56:42,433 --> 00:56:44,780
-Thank you.
-You must eat something.

1581
00:56:44,815 --> 00:56:46,057
Do you feel all right?

1582
00:56:46,092 --> 00:56:48,957
-Oh, don't light a match
is all I'll say.

1583
00:56:48,991 --> 00:56:50,510
-The poor man suffers so.

1584
00:56:50,545 --> 00:56:51,580
-I'm from the 19th century.

1585
00:56:51,615 --> 00:56:53,893
What does he want with me?

1586
00:56:53,927 --> 00:56:55,515
-Bad news,
all out of curly fries.

1587
00:56:55,550 --> 00:56:56,620
-The chief wants you.

1588
00:56:56,654 --> 00:56:57,828
-In the worst way.

1589
00:56:57,862 --> 00:56:59,450
-We were just about
to begin eating.

1590
00:56:59,485 --> 00:57:00,624
-You'll eat later.

1591
00:57:00,658 --> 00:57:01,970
-And me.

1592
00:57:05,111 --> 00:57:06,181
-What's the matter, you?

1593
00:57:06,215 --> 00:57:07,458
Isn't our food
good enough for you?

1594
00:57:07,493 --> 00:57:09,702
-Uh, no.
-Come on, on your feet, you!

1595
00:57:09,736 --> 00:57:11,220
-Ah, ah, ah!

1596
00:57:11,255 --> 00:57:13,464
-The man is sick.
Leave him alone!

1597
00:57:13,499 --> 00:57:14,534
-On your feet, you!

1598
00:57:14,569 --> 00:57:16,156
-But he's a sick man!
Oh!

1599
00:57:16,191 --> 00:57:17,848
-Oi, he waved his
stinky foot at me!

1600
00:57:17,882 --> 00:57:19,746
-Come on, eat this!

1601
00:57:19,781 --> 00:57:21,161
Eat it, I tell you!

1602
00:57:21,196 --> 00:57:22,577
-No.

1603
00:57:22,611 --> 00:57:24,164
-Ah, Mr. Bond, Bach.

1604
00:57:24,199 --> 00:57:28,168
-Ah, good morning, gentlemen.
You slept well, I hope?

1605
00:57:28,203 --> 00:57:30,308
-Yes, in my double-breasted
sleeping suit and tie.

1606
00:57:30,343 --> 00:57:33,035
-Tell him about how
we were about to eat.

1607
00:57:33,070 --> 00:57:36,556
-Listen, I speak formy colleagues as well as myself.

1608
00:57:36,591 --> 00:57:38,938
It is impossible to agree
to your demands.

1609
00:57:38,972 --> 00:57:39,835
-What?

1610
00:57:39,870 --> 00:57:41,734
-We are only men of science.

1611
00:57:41,768 --> 00:57:44,288
We can explain to our people
the state of your technology,

1612
00:57:44,322 --> 00:57:45,738
but we cannot
accept responsibility

1613
00:57:45,772 --> 00:57:47,015
for making political decisions.

1614
00:57:47,049 --> 00:57:48,637
-Who's talking?
-I understand...

1615
00:57:48,672 --> 00:57:49,845
-Again.
-I don't know.

1616
00:57:49,880 --> 00:57:51,226
-...though I cannot comprehend
a civilization

1617
00:57:51,260 --> 00:57:52,469
where intelligent men
like yourselves...

1618
00:57:52,503 --> 00:57:53,918
-Hello?

1619
00:57:53,953 --> 00:57:56,024
-...are not permitted to guide
the destinies of their people.

1620
00:57:56,058 --> 00:57:57,232
-Very well, then.

1621
00:57:57,266 --> 00:58:00,200
You agree to describe
our technology,

1622
00:58:00,235 --> 00:58:02,548
and you will do it so well
that even your government heads

1623
00:58:02,582 --> 00:58:05,033
will realize the hopelessness
of opposing me.

1624
00:58:05,067 --> 00:58:06,310
-Mm-hmm.
-All righty then.

1625
00:58:06,344 --> 00:58:07,587
-You'll make the necessary
arrangements,

1626
00:58:07,622 --> 00:58:09,140
then, to send us back to Earth?

1627
00:58:09,175 --> 00:58:10,901
-No need of that.

1628
00:58:10,935 --> 00:58:13,490
You can broadcast your message
directly from here.

1629
00:58:13,524 --> 00:58:15,526
-That means that we --
-That's right.

1630
00:58:15,561 --> 00:58:17,977
You may expect to remain
with us for some time...

1631
00:58:18,011 --> 00:58:19,461
-Oh.
-Gasp!

1632
00:58:19,496 --> 00:58:21,601
-...until you have assisted me
with all my plans.

1633
00:58:21,636 --> 00:58:24,086
-Bryce, when will I see you
again, Bryce?

1634
00:58:24,121 --> 00:58:28,401
♪♪

1635
00:58:28,435 --> 00:58:30,679
-I'm going to mess you up, mmm.

1636
00:58:30,714 --> 00:58:34,096
♪♪

1637
00:58:34,131 --> 00:58:35,753
-Beautiful, just beautiful.

1638
00:58:35,788 --> 00:58:37,444
-Mm.

1639
00:58:37,479 --> 00:58:39,550
The Cabrini Green of Japan.

1640
00:58:39,585 --> 00:58:41,863
♪♪

1641
00:58:41,897 --> 00:58:45,970
What if it's just a really
slow chase scene with one car?

1642
00:58:46,005 --> 00:58:50,216
♪♪

1643
00:58:50,250 --> 00:58:53,840
-What, are we driving through
plutonium?

1644
00:58:53,875 --> 00:58:55,462
-It's Garbo.

1645
00:58:55,497 --> 00:58:56,912
-Hey, hey, wake up!

1646
00:58:56,947 --> 00:58:58,742
-Bawk, bawk, bawk.

1647
00:58:58,776 --> 00:59:00,502
-Be careful, I don't think
the chief would like it

1648
00:59:00,537 --> 00:59:02,608
if he knew
you were sleeping on the job.

1649
00:59:05,611 --> 00:59:09,200
-Hey, wake up,
your egg is hatching.

1650
00:59:09,235 --> 00:59:10,477
-What is it?

1651
00:59:10,512 --> 00:59:11,927
-That's better.

1652
00:59:11,962 --> 00:59:14,896
You heard anything from
the flagship, from the chief?

1653
00:59:14,930 --> 00:59:16,829
-Not since they passed through
the meteors, no.

1654
00:59:16,863 --> 00:59:18,106
-All right.
Stay awake!

1655
00:59:18,140 --> 00:59:19,659
-Yeah, blow it
out your gizzard.

1656
00:59:19,694 --> 00:59:21,316
-Nothing new.

1657
00:59:21,350 --> 00:59:23,387
We'd better get some kind of
a lead on that prince

1658
00:59:23,421 --> 00:59:25,700
before the chief gets here.

1659
00:59:25,734 --> 00:59:29,220
Sure is funny how he disappearedwithout a trace, his car too.

1660
00:59:29,255 --> 00:59:30,256
-Get out of the way!

1661
00:59:30,290 --> 00:59:31,429
-The police have been
looking for him.

1662
00:59:31,464 --> 00:59:33,570
-I know.
-But they don't know anything.

1663
00:59:33,604 --> 00:59:34,881
The commissioner told me
they figured

1664
00:59:34,916 --> 00:59:36,780
it must have been the spacemen.

1665
00:59:36,814 --> 00:59:39,403
I guess so.
It's the only explanation.

1666
00:59:41,612 --> 00:59:42,579
-Hold it!

1667
00:59:42,613 --> 00:59:43,856
-My Slurpee spilled!

1668
00:59:43,890 --> 00:59:47,307
-Pick up something?
-Uh-huh.

1669
00:59:47,342 --> 00:59:50,863
I just got a reading
on the meter.

1670
00:59:50,897 --> 00:59:51,933
-Okay, right foot.

1671
00:59:51,967 --> 00:59:54,591
-All right.
Don't work so fast.

1672
00:59:58,456 --> 01:00:00,079
-Are you ever going
to stop farting?

1673
01:00:00,113 --> 01:00:02,322
Is that even
a remote possibility?

1674
01:00:04,152 --> 01:00:06,603
-That's close enough.
Cut in the automatic search.

1675
01:00:08,328 --> 01:00:10,089
-[Humming "Pop Goes the Weasel"]

1676
01:00:10,123 --> 01:00:12,781
-Well, Nomo got shelled
again last night.

1677
01:00:12,816 --> 01:00:18,028
♪♪

1678
01:00:18,062 --> 01:00:20,064
-Get back to work,
or you're back on the street!

1679
01:00:20,099 --> 01:00:22,826
-Fast hands.

1680
01:00:22,860 --> 01:00:24,759
-It's the shoeshine boy.

1681
01:00:24,793 --> 01:00:26,795
-Put it on the beam.
-Right.

1682
01:00:28,245 --> 01:00:30,247
[Beeping]

1683
01:00:30,281 --> 01:00:32,318
-Attention -- X-radar gave...
-Whee!

1684
01:00:32,352 --> 01:00:36,391
-...a very high rating of 98
on shoeshine boy.

1685
01:00:36,425 --> 01:00:37,634
-Tune it in properly!

1686
01:00:37,668 --> 01:00:39,463
-Just wiggle it around!

1687
01:00:43,570 --> 01:00:45,193
-Check, please.

1688
01:00:48,403 --> 01:00:50,716
-Would you mind
if I paid you in Tic Tacs?

1689
01:00:54,478 --> 01:00:55,513
-Heh.

1690
01:00:55,548 --> 01:00:56,894
-Ha-ha, so our Prince of Space

1691
01:00:56,929 --> 01:01:00,449
is disguised as
a miserable boot-black, clever.

1692
01:01:00,484 --> 01:01:03,556
We never would have picked
him up without the X-radar.

1693
01:01:03,590 --> 01:01:04,971
Attention, Earth Patrol --

1694
01:01:05,006 --> 01:01:07,249
This is your commander
speaking personally to you.

1695
01:01:07,284 --> 01:01:08,423
-Ba-kawk.

1696
01:01:08,457 --> 01:01:09,735
-Now that you have found
this Prince of Space,

1697
01:01:09,769 --> 01:01:12,599
be careful and keep him 
in sight at all times.

1698
01:01:12,634 --> 01:01:15,879
-Careful, he'll try to sell you
you shoelaces with your shine!

1699
01:01:15,913 --> 01:01:17,156
-You heard what he said.

1700
01:01:17,190 --> 01:01:18,122
-Yeah.

1701
01:01:18,157 --> 01:01:19,710
-Whatever.

1702
01:01:19,745 --> 01:01:22,575
-Can I just learn to read,and then I'll come back to work?

1703
01:01:24,611 --> 01:01:26,786
-I got to boot-black
down at the track.

1704
01:01:26,821 --> 01:01:30,203
Yep, big boot-blacking thing
going on.

1705
01:01:30,238 --> 01:01:31,895
-Hey, boot-black,
congratulations!

1706
01:01:31,929 --> 01:01:33,966
When are you due?

1707
01:01:34,000 --> 01:01:37,038
-Mr. Tannin!
Hey, Mr. Tannin!

1708
01:01:37,072 --> 01:01:38,280
-Get out of my wine.

1709
01:01:38,315 --> 01:01:39,730
-You forgot this.

1710
01:01:39,765 --> 01:01:41,663
You're getting absentminded.

1711
01:01:41,698 --> 01:01:42,768
-Thanks.
-Be healed!

1712
01:01:42,802 --> 01:01:44,701
-[Laughs]

1713
01:01:44,735 --> 01:01:46,150
-[Chuckles]

1714
01:01:46,185 --> 01:01:48,705
-Man, I hate that
bastard, geez!

1715
01:01:48,739 --> 01:01:52,260
♪♪

1716
01:01:52,294 --> 01:01:56,091
-You, uh, carry 
Boot-Black Journal,yeah?

1717
01:01:56,126 --> 01:01:58,922
Ah, here it is -- 
Little Baby Sun Hatsmonthly!

1718
01:02:01,027 --> 01:02:01,959
-Scalpel.

1719
01:02:01,994 --> 01:02:02,995
-What happened?

1720
01:02:03,029 --> 01:02:04,859
-He ran away.

1721
01:02:04,893 --> 01:02:06,205
He came back.

1722
01:02:06,239 --> 01:02:07,309
It's all right now.

1723
01:02:07,344 --> 01:02:09,208
-No, wait.
He ran away again.

1724
01:02:09,242 --> 01:02:12,142
-Attention, Earth Patrol.
Attention.

1725
01:02:12,176 --> 01:02:13,350
-Oh, what's this?

1726
01:02:13,384 --> 01:02:16,077
-We will arrive
over the city in 30 seconds.

1727
01:02:16,111 --> 01:02:18,769
-You better clean
this place up!

1728
01:02:18,804 --> 01:02:20,564
-Report any suspicious
movements

1729
01:02:20,598 --> 01:02:21,979
when we appear in the sky.

1730
01:02:22,014 --> 01:02:24,085
-I had a suspicious movement
after breakfast.

1731
01:02:24,119 --> 01:02:25,534
-All right.
-Oh, no. Great.

1732
01:02:25,569 --> 01:02:27,605
-Take her down.
-Right, sir.

1733
01:02:27,640 --> 01:02:30,298
-Full descent to 500 feet.

1734
01:02:30,332 --> 01:02:32,645
-Set hull fryers to stun!

1735
01:02:34,854 --> 01:02:35,924
[Man shouts]

1736
01:02:35,959 --> 01:02:37,788
-The upper half
of a Hopper painting.

1737
01:02:37,823 --> 01:02:39,031
[All shouting]

1738
01:02:39,065 --> 01:02:40,515
-Ah! A giant roast chicken!

1739
01:02:40,549 --> 01:02:42,931
-It is brown on the outside,
tender and juicy on the inside!

1740
01:02:42,966 --> 01:02:45,313
-It is not fermented,
pickled, or raw! Run!

1741
01:02:45,347 --> 01:02:47,798
-Oh!
-Potatoes or stuffing?

1742
01:02:47,833 --> 01:02:51,871
[All shouting]

1743
01:02:51,906 --> 01:02:56,082
-♪ When I was Japanese,
it was a very good year ♪

1744
01:02:56,117 --> 01:02:57,635
[All shouting]

1745
01:02:57,670 --> 01:02:59,534
-Oh! Ice dams!

1746
01:02:59,568 --> 01:03:02,502
We have ice dams!

1747
01:03:02,537 --> 01:03:03,849
-It may not be relevant,

1748
01:03:03,883 --> 01:03:05,816
but did you know that Gamera
is friend to children?

1749
01:03:05,851 --> 01:03:07,680
-Gamera? Ah, he is made
of turtle meat, right?

1750
01:03:07,714 --> 01:03:09,268
-Yes, he is really neat.

1751
01:03:09,302 --> 01:03:13,755
[All shouting]

1752
01:03:13,790 --> 01:03:16,585
-I like that very much.

1753
01:03:16,862 --> 01:03:21,418
♪♪

1754
01:03:22,626 --> 01:03:24,524
-Sir, they called us "weenies."

1755
01:03:24,559 --> 01:03:26,975
-Sir, we are ready
with the all-wave transmitter.

1756
01:03:27,010 --> 01:03:28,632
-Yes.

1757
01:03:28,666 --> 01:03:32,153
-Uh, sir, you left an egg
on the chair.

1758
01:03:32,187 --> 01:03:33,844
-Give me the microphone.

1759
01:03:33,879 --> 01:03:35,225
Put Professor Macken
on the screen.

1760
01:03:35,259 --> 01:03:37,365
-The camera loves him!

1761
01:03:37,399 --> 01:03:39,539
-Attention, people of Earth,

1762
01:03:39,574 --> 01:03:41,818
I have an important
announcement to make,

1763
01:03:41,852 --> 01:03:43,854
one that you've been
waiting for a long time.

1764
01:03:43,889 --> 01:03:45,097
-Yeah!

1765
01:03:45,131 --> 01:03:46,408
-Up here with me,

1766
01:03:46,443 --> 01:03:48,514
I have the famous
Professor Macken...

1767
01:03:48,548 --> 01:03:49,791
-Hmm.

1768
01:03:49,826 --> 01:03:51,241
-...a name you all recognize,

1769
01:03:51,275 --> 01:03:55,314
who has agreed to speak to you
on my behalf.

1770
01:03:55,348 --> 01:03:56,315
Go ahead, professor.

1771
01:03:56,349 --> 01:03:58,558
-Hey, the Japanese Sylvia Plath.

1772
01:03:58,593 --> 01:04:00,146
-For the past 24 hours,

1773
01:04:00,181 --> 01:04:03,184
I and several of my colleagues 
have been captives

1774
01:04:03,218 --> 01:04:06,497
aboard the flagship 
of the person who just spoke,

1775
01:04:06,532 --> 01:04:07,878
the dictator of Krankor.

1776
01:04:07,913 --> 01:04:08,983
-Oh!

1777
01:04:09,017 --> 01:04:11,054
-For most of that time, 
we have been...

1778
01:04:11,088 --> 01:04:12,710
-Where's his chin?
It's gone.

1779
01:04:12,745 --> 01:04:15,886
-...captive witnesses of his 
state of military technology

1780
01:04:15,921 --> 01:04:17,750
capable of destroying any of

1781
01:04:17,784 --> 01:04:19,994
the great metropolitan 
centers of Earth.

1782
01:04:20,028 --> 01:04:22,720
In order to demonstrate 
his power,

1783
01:04:22,755 --> 01:04:25,171
the dictator intends 
to wipe out one of our cities

1784
01:04:25,206 --> 01:04:26,517
at noon tomorrow.

1785
01:04:26,552 --> 01:04:28,899
The only way to prevent this

1786
01:04:28,934 --> 01:04:30,797
is for all nations 
and all the governments

1787
01:04:30,832 --> 01:04:32,316
of this planet

1788
01:04:32,351 --> 01:04:35,561
to agree to accept his terms 
for unconditional surrender!

1789
01:04:35,595 --> 01:04:37,011
People of Earth, listen to me!

1790
01:04:37,045 --> 01:04:39,358
You have only one response 
to make --

1791
01:04:39,392 --> 01:04:40,393
bomb the -- ah!

1792
01:04:40,428 --> 01:04:42,533
-Bomb the aye-re-raw?
-Very good.

1793
01:04:42,568 --> 01:04:43,845
-Aye-re-raw!

1794
01:04:43,880 --> 01:04:44,811
-Put him back in his quarters.

1795
01:04:44,846 --> 01:04:45,916
-Get him some tights.

1796
01:04:45,951 --> 01:04:47,918
-Put me on the screen.
-Right, sir.

1797
01:04:47,953 --> 01:04:49,816
-Come on.
This way.

1798
01:04:49,851 --> 01:04:51,991
Get going.

1799
01:04:52,026 --> 01:04:53,303
-All right.

1800
01:04:53,337 --> 01:04:55,892
As you can see, 
your professor is indisposed,

1801
01:04:55,926 --> 01:04:56,962
so I will address 
you personally.

1802
01:04:56,996 --> 01:04:58,170
-Darling, this is fun.

1803
01:04:58,204 --> 01:04:59,792
-Go faster?

1804
01:04:59,826 --> 01:05:01,276
Raise your hand
if you'd like to go faster.

1805
01:05:01,311 --> 01:05:04,038
-I'm sitting in the command 
center of my flagship,

1806
01:05:04,072 --> 01:05:06,833
and, as professor Macken 
has told you, if I so wished,

1807
01:05:06,868 --> 01:05:08,318
I could at this very moment

1808
01:05:08,352 --> 01:05:10,458
wipe your entire city 
off the map.

1809
01:05:10,492 --> 01:05:11,942
-Turn to "Full House." 
-I could do the same

1810
01:05:11,977 --> 01:05:15,256
to New York, Paris, 
Rome, Berlin, Moscow,

1811
01:05:15,290 --> 01:05:17,189
all of your great 
metropolitan centers.

1812
01:05:17,223 --> 01:05:18,190
-Pop, pop music.

1813
01:05:18,224 --> 01:05:20,019
-You can do nothing to stop me,

1814
01:05:20,054 --> 01:05:21,641
for I have completed paralyzed

1815
01:05:21,676 --> 01:05:23,781
all of your primitive 
defense measures.

1816
01:05:23,816 --> 01:05:25,714
Your radar cannot find me.

1817
01:05:25,749 --> 01:05:27,993
Your fastest jet planes 
would be destroyed

1818
01:05:28,027 --> 01:05:29,787
the moment they approached 
my headquarters.

1819
01:05:29,822 --> 01:05:31,341
-What the hell is this?

1820
01:05:31,375 --> 01:05:32,790
-So you are wise to keep 
your war planes grounded

1821
01:05:32,825 --> 01:05:34,861
and listen to me 
quietly and calmly.

1822
01:05:34,896 --> 01:05:36,794
-Oh, maybe?

1823
01:05:36,829 --> 01:05:37,968
-I have come to offer you 
a choice

1824
01:05:38,003 --> 01:05:40,660
between peace 
or extermination.

1825
01:05:40,695 --> 01:05:43,905
If you do not accept my demand 
for unconditional surrender,

1826
01:05:43,940 --> 01:05:44,975
I will destroy you.

1827
01:05:45,010 --> 01:05:46,425
-Oh!
-Oh.

1828
01:05:46,459 --> 01:05:48,496
-But if you accept me 
willingly as your ruler,

1829
01:05:48,530 --> 01:05:50,291
your entire planet 
will enter upon

1830
01:05:50,325 --> 01:05:51,982
a period of peace 
and prosperity

1831
01:05:52,017 --> 01:05:54,640
such as it has never known 
in all its recorded history.

1832
01:05:54,674 --> 01:05:56,159
-Okay, we give in.

1833
01:05:56,193 --> 01:05:57,470
-You have 24 hours

1834
01:05:57,505 --> 01:05:59,748
to make your wishes 
known to me.

1835
01:05:59,783 --> 01:06:02,544
I will return tomorrow.

1836
01:06:02,579 --> 01:06:04,857
You will tell me then whether 
you prefer to surrender...

1837
01:06:04,891 --> 01:06:05,927
-♪ Ba, ba, boom
Ba, boom ♪

1838
01:06:05,962 --> 01:06:07,756
-...or die.

1839
01:06:07,791 --> 01:06:10,449
[Laughs]

1840
01:06:10,483 --> 01:06:13,659
-Oh, and we need worms.

1841
01:06:13,693 --> 01:06:15,764
[Buzzing]

1842
01:06:15,799 --> 01:06:19,423
-It's going to rain
giblets on us!

1843
01:06:19,458 --> 01:06:21,080
-The Prince of Indecision.

1844
01:06:24,359 --> 01:06:26,292
-Wally, come on.
Let's get out of here, Wally.

1845
01:06:26,327 --> 01:06:29,157
Come on.

1846
01:06:29,192 --> 01:06:31,677
-Well, back into
the fart-mobile.

1847
01:06:31,711 --> 01:06:34,438
I still like boot-blacking
very much.

1848
01:06:34,473 --> 01:06:37,510
♪♪

1849
01:06:37,545 --> 01:06:38,856
Ba-kawk!

1850
01:06:38,891 --> 01:06:40,410
-Come on, slave labor.

1851
01:06:40,444 --> 01:06:42,653
I mean kids, kids, kids.

1852
01:06:46,381 --> 01:06:49,039
-Chief, Prince is walking away.

1853
01:06:49,074 --> 01:06:50,454
We'll follow him.

1854
01:06:50,489 --> 01:06:51,973
Go on, follow him!

1855
01:06:52,008 --> 01:06:53,147
-Stay with him.

1856
01:06:53,181 --> 01:06:54,734
Don't let him 
out of your sight.

1857
01:06:54,769 --> 01:06:56,909
But above all, don't let
him know you are following.

1858
01:06:56,943 --> 01:06:58,014
-Bock, bock, bock.

1859
01:06:58,048 --> 01:06:59,291
-I will be there tonight,

1860
01:06:59,325 --> 01:07:00,706
and I want to be able 
to take him at once.

1861
01:07:00,740 --> 01:07:02,880
-Do you ever get the feeling
Krankor is just winging it?

1862
01:07:02,915 --> 01:07:04,537
-Oh, yeah.

1863
01:07:06,608 --> 01:07:09,473
-We'll go to a land where
we are free to boot-black.

1864
01:07:09,508 --> 01:07:14,892
♪♪

1865
01:07:14,927 --> 01:07:18,172
-Bawk, bawk.

1866
01:07:18,206 --> 01:07:19,449
-My egg is crowning!

1867
01:07:19,483 --> 01:07:20,622
-I wonder how far
he's going to walk.

1868
01:07:20,657 --> 01:07:23,073
-Until we stop following him.

1869
01:07:23,108 --> 01:07:24,074
-Never mind the jokes.

1870
01:07:24,109 --> 01:07:25,317
-Sorry for my zaniness.

1871
01:07:25,351 --> 01:07:27,043
-They're going into the house.

1872
01:07:27,077 --> 01:07:31,254
♪♪

1873
01:07:31,288 --> 01:07:33,394
-I am going to
boot-black in my room.

1874
01:07:33,428 --> 01:07:37,363
♪♪

1875
01:07:37,398 --> 01:07:39,779
-Kimmy, don't eat
all the jellied squid!

1876
01:07:39,814 --> 01:07:42,575
♪♪

1877
01:07:42,610 --> 01:07:44,232
-Cram it, world.

1878
01:07:49,444 --> 01:07:52,275
-Ah, home at last!

1879
01:07:52,309 --> 01:07:54,311
Good boy, Mickey.
Going to feed the bird, huh?

1880
01:07:54,346 --> 01:07:55,933
-What difference does it make
if that mean dictator

1881
01:07:55,968 --> 01:07:58,246
is going
to burn us all up anyhow?

1882
01:07:58,281 --> 01:07:59,385
-Where is the Prince of Space?

1883
01:07:59,420 --> 01:08:01,111
He's the only one
who could help us.

1884
01:08:01,146 --> 01:08:02,112
-Don't worry, Mickey.

1885
01:08:02,147 --> 01:08:03,458
He will surely help us out.

1886
01:08:03,493 --> 01:08:05,943
-You think so?
-Of course he will!

1887
01:08:05,978 --> 01:08:09,050
He always came before, right?
Didn't he, Mickey?

1888
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:11,949
-Oh, I think he's gone away
and forgotten about us.

1889
01:08:11,984 --> 01:08:13,641
-That bird left
a letter of resignation.

1890
01:08:13,675 --> 01:08:15,125
-Hey!

1891
01:08:15,160 --> 01:08:16,782
-Leave 50 cuttlebones
under the bridge,

1892
01:08:16,816 --> 01:08:18,301
or I start spotting your car.

1893
01:08:18,335 --> 01:08:20,475
-It's for me.
"Dear Mickey,

1894
01:08:20,510 --> 01:08:23,202
go to Johnnie's house
right away with your sister."

1895
01:08:23,237 --> 01:08:25,549
Signed Prince of Space.

1896
01:08:25,584 --> 01:08:27,586
Hey, Wally, what do
you think about that?

1897
01:08:27,620 --> 01:08:29,450
-Let's do what the note
says, Mickey.

1898
01:08:29,484 --> 01:08:30,727
-No, wait a minute.

1899
01:08:30,761 --> 01:08:33,212
Who could put a note
like this up on the cage?

1900
01:08:33,247 --> 01:08:34,455
-Never mind that!
Get a move on!

1901
01:08:34,489 --> 01:08:35,628
-What?

1902
01:08:35,663 --> 01:08:36,733
-You want to do what the note
says, right?

1903
01:08:36,767 --> 01:08:37,803
-Right, yeah.

1904
01:08:37,837 --> 01:08:38,873
Come on. Let's go.

1905
01:08:38,907 --> 01:08:40,116
-Whoa.
-All right. Goodbye, Wally.

1906
01:08:40,150 --> 01:08:41,703
Don't worry about us.
Go on with your dinner.

1907
01:08:41,738 --> 01:08:43,049
-Hurry, Kimmy, come on!

1908
01:08:43,084 --> 01:08:44,741
-The kid's great.
I love that kid.

1909
01:08:44,775 --> 01:08:46,846
-Wow.

1910
01:08:46,881 --> 01:08:49,987
-Finally, an evening alone
together!

1911
01:08:50,022 --> 01:08:51,092
-Oh!
-Oh!

1912
01:08:51,127 --> 01:08:52,128
-We got chickens!

1913
01:08:53,612 --> 01:08:54,716
-Bawk, bawk.

1914
01:08:54,751 --> 01:08:58,651
-I don't want to be
Prince of Space!

1915
01:08:58,686 --> 01:08:59,618
-Wait, where are you going?

1916
01:08:59,652 --> 01:09:01,999
Come back
and let us capture you!

1917
01:09:02,034 --> 01:09:03,794
-Bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk!
-Bah, bah, bawk, bawk, bawk!

1918
01:09:03,829 --> 01:09:07,557
-Bawk, bawk, bawk, baah, bawk!
-Bah, bah, bawk, bah.

1919
01:09:07,591 --> 01:09:08,903
♪♪

1920
01:09:08,937 --> 01:09:12,078
-Exotic locations like
Normandale Community College!

1921
01:09:12,113 --> 01:09:13,666
-The chief is on his way
to meet us.

1922
01:09:13,701 --> 01:09:15,875
What are we going to do?-Just keep the radio beam going.

1923
01:09:15,910 --> 01:09:16,738
-Bawk.

1924
01:09:16,773 --> 01:09:17,877
♪♪

1925
01:09:17,912 --> 01:09:19,741
-Prince of Hauling Ass, whoo!

1926
01:09:19,776 --> 01:09:21,571
-Halt, or we fire.

1927
01:09:23,607 --> 01:09:24,712
-Well, his sights are pulling

1928
01:09:24,746 --> 01:09:27,715
about 60 yards
to the left there.

1929
01:09:27,749 --> 01:09:29,751
-Bawk, bawk, bah-bawk,
bah-ca-bawk!

1930
01:09:29,786 --> 01:09:31,097
-Ba-cah!
-Ba-cah, ba-cah, bah, bah!

1931
01:09:31,132 --> 01:09:33,030
-Bah-bah, bawk, bawk!

1932
01:09:33,065 --> 01:09:35,032
-I brought grubworms
for everyone!

1933
01:09:37,483 --> 01:09:38,691
-After him.
That way!

1934
01:09:38,726 --> 01:09:41,418
-Deploy your tiny whippers
only if necessary.

1935
01:09:41,453 --> 01:09:45,388
♪♪

1936
01:09:45,422 --> 01:09:46,768
-Maybe they just came
to this planet

1937
01:09:46,803 --> 01:09:49,495
to serve the guy a subpoena.

1938
01:09:49,530 --> 01:09:50,772
Maybe not.

1939
01:09:50,807 --> 01:09:54,086
♪♪

1940
01:09:54,120 --> 01:09:55,432
-Bawk, bawk.

1941
01:09:55,467 --> 01:09:59,574
-Even in death, they're stacked
on top of each other.

1942
01:09:59,609 --> 01:10:01,680
-Bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk,
bawk-bawk!

1943
01:10:02,957 --> 01:10:04,130
-Ooh.

1944
01:10:04,165 --> 01:10:06,098
-Ba-kawk.

1945
01:10:06,132 --> 01:10:07,099
Bawk, bawk.

1946
01:10:07,133 --> 01:10:09,101
-Oh, Prince of Space!

1947
01:10:09,135 --> 01:10:10,999
-I was thinking it was going
to be Fritz Mondale,

1948
01:10:11,034 --> 01:10:14,589
but of course
it's Prince of Space.

1949
01:10:14,624 --> 01:10:15,590
-Hold your fire!

1950
01:10:15,625 --> 01:10:18,144
-You guys look ridiculous!

1951
01:10:18,179 --> 01:10:19,525
-Your weapons are useless.

1952
01:10:19,560 --> 01:10:21,078
Let's try bare hands now.

1953
01:10:21,113 --> 01:10:22,252
-Argh!

1954
01:10:22,287 --> 01:10:24,392
-I pound on Prince's face!

1955
01:10:24,427 --> 01:10:25,842
-His power apparently lies

1956
01:10:25,876 --> 01:10:28,431
in his choosing
incompetent enemies.

1957
01:10:28,465 --> 01:10:30,812
♪♪

1958
01:10:30,847 --> 01:10:32,780
-The Mertzes are here!
We're saved!

1959
01:10:32,814 --> 01:10:34,402
♪♪

1960
01:10:34,437 --> 01:10:36,542
-My mom is here.
I got to go.

1961
01:10:36,577 --> 01:10:39,856
♪♪

1962
01:10:39,890 --> 01:10:42,203
-The hell?

1963
01:10:42,238 --> 01:10:44,999
-Oh, hi. Charity, huh?

1964
01:10:45,033 --> 01:10:46,311
-You again?

1965
01:10:46,345 --> 01:10:47,898
-Ha, ha, yes, it's me.

1966
01:10:47,933 --> 01:10:49,072
-Heh, ha!

1967
01:10:49,106 --> 01:10:50,798
-I've come to finish you off.

1968
01:10:50,832 --> 01:10:52,317
-What a vicious cycle.

1969
01:10:54,595 --> 01:10:56,321
-Eh, I figure
he'll get bored and die,

1970
01:10:56,355 --> 01:10:59,013
and then I will rule, heh-heh!

1971
01:10:59,047 --> 01:11:01,291
♪♪

1972
01:11:01,326 --> 01:11:04,881
-Ah, even I am beginning
to doubt my powers.

1973
01:11:04,915 --> 01:11:06,331
-Ha, ha, ha, ha!

1974
01:11:06,365 --> 01:11:07,504
You see?

1975
01:11:07,539 --> 01:11:09,506
How many times do I have
to demonstrate to you --

1976
01:11:09,541 --> 01:11:10,852
Your guns are worthless
against me!

1977
01:11:10,887 --> 01:11:12,060
-Infinite.

1978
01:11:12,095 --> 01:11:13,303
-Come closer.

1979
01:11:13,338 --> 01:11:15,305
-I'm close enough.
Thank you anyway.

1980
01:11:15,340 --> 01:11:16,479
The stench of your foul breath

1981
01:11:16,513 --> 01:11:17,894
is more than
my stomach can stand.

1982
01:11:17,928 --> 01:11:18,826
-Wow.
-Chief, let's go!

1983
01:11:18,860 --> 01:11:19,792
-Get away!

1984
01:11:19,827 --> 01:11:22,001
Fire! Fire!

1985
01:11:22,036 --> 01:11:23,037
-Oh.

1986
01:11:23,071 --> 01:11:24,141
Sorry, sir.

1987
01:11:24,176 --> 01:11:27,317
You do have bad breath,
you know.

1988
01:11:27,352 --> 01:11:29,077
-I feel good all under!

1989
01:11:31,459 --> 01:11:33,530
-Oh, boy. Hey, wait up!
I need a ride!

1990
01:11:33,565 --> 01:11:34,807
I didn't mean that
about your breath.

1991
01:11:34,842 --> 01:11:35,981
Come on!

1992
01:11:36,015 --> 01:11:40,779
♪♪

1993
01:11:40,813 --> 01:11:43,644
-Chief, in the stern window
of that flying saucer.

1994
01:11:43,678 --> 01:11:46,543
-It's Mir, limping
into a service station.

1995
01:11:46,578 --> 01:11:48,234
-What do we do?
-Get them out of here.

1996
01:11:48,269 --> 01:11:50,167
Put them in their quarters.
Do it!

1997
01:11:50,202 --> 01:11:51,790
-All right.
-Back to your rooms.

1998
01:11:51,824 --> 01:11:53,964
-Chickens are too stupid
to mutiny.

1999
01:11:53,999 --> 01:11:58,348
♪♪

2000
01:11:58,383 --> 01:12:00,833
-My chest-mounted soap dish
will help me.

2001
01:12:00,868 --> 01:12:02,007
-Bawk, bawk.

2002
01:12:02,041 --> 01:12:03,284
-What are we going
to do, chief?

2003
01:12:03,319 --> 01:12:04,458
-Bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk.

2004
01:12:04,492 --> 01:12:06,011
-That tin can will never
survive another trip

2005
01:12:06,045 --> 01:12:07,115
through the meteor zone.

2006
01:12:07,150 --> 01:12:08,393
-Bah, bawk, bawk, bawk, bawk.
-Oh?

2007
01:12:08,427 --> 01:12:10,326
-But just to make sure,
prepare the caustic vapor!

2008
01:12:21,992 --> 01:12:24,823
[Birds chirping]

2009
01:12:24,857 --> 01:12:26,203
-Well, this is good, huh?

2010
01:12:26,238 --> 01:12:27,895
Okay, everything seems
to be back to normal.

2011
01:12:27,929 --> 01:12:31,450
I'm a flesh and human being,
and you guys are...

2012
01:12:31,485 --> 01:12:32,658
Oh, no.

2013
01:12:33,487 --> 01:12:36,179
Oh, no!

2014
01:12:36,213 --> 01:12:39,769
-Uh, Mike,
why are we in a sylvan glen?

2015
01:12:39,803 --> 01:12:41,495
-[Sneezes, coughs]

2016
01:12:41,529 --> 01:12:43,151
Hey, I got hay fever!
Cool!

2017
01:12:43,186 --> 01:12:44,290
[Laughs]

2018
01:12:44,325 --> 01:12:45,568
-I'm going to --

2019
01:12:45,602 --> 01:12:47,915
I'm going to go lay down
until this all blows over.

2020
01:12:47,949 --> 01:12:51,574
I'll -- I'll see you later.
-Uh, I -- I may need a Kleenex!

2021
01:12:51,608 --> 01:12:53,196
-You're fine.

2022
01:12:53,230 --> 01:12:55,336
-[Sniffles, coughs]

2023
01:12:55,371 --> 01:12:56,820
-Poor guy.
-Yeah.

2024
01:12:56,855 --> 01:13:00,168
-He doesn't handle alternate
realities very well, does he?

2025
01:13:00,203 --> 01:13:01,515
-[Sneezes]

2026
01:13:01,549 --> 01:13:02,930
Sorry, heh.

2027
01:13:03,413 --> 01:13:05,001
Ah, uh.

2028
01:13:05,035 --> 01:13:06,312
-Hmm.

2029
01:13:06,347 --> 01:13:09,419
Still, it's a nice day though.
Yeah.

2030
01:13:09,454 --> 01:13:10,489
-Yeah, yup.

2031
01:13:12,249 --> 01:13:13,492
-Hmm.

2032
01:13:13,527 --> 01:13:15,736
-Fishing?

2033
01:13:19,705 --> 01:13:24,572
♪♪

2034
01:13:25,608 --> 01:13:27,092
-Oh, you okay?
-Yeah.

2035
01:13:27,126 --> 01:13:28,507
Oh, God.

2036
01:13:28,542 --> 01:13:29,991
-Look, he's heading right
for the center.

2037
01:13:30,026 --> 01:13:32,062
Those meteorites will pound him
to pieces in a few minutes!

2038
01:13:32,097 --> 01:13:33,995
[Laughs]

2039
01:13:34,030 --> 01:13:36,066
-Yep, I'm the man.

2040
01:13:36,101 --> 01:13:37,240
-All right.

2041
01:13:37,274 --> 01:13:38,966
I think we've seen
the last of him.

2042
01:13:39,000 --> 01:13:41,486
He'll never come out
of that alive.

2043
01:13:41,520 --> 01:13:43,591
-Ah.
-Give everyone 4 hours off.

2044
01:13:43,626 --> 01:13:44,558
[Laughter]

2045
01:13:44,592 --> 01:13:45,766
-In the morning,
we'll return to Earth...

2046
01:13:45,800 --> 01:13:46,974
-Sir, did you forget something
when you got

2047
01:13:47,008 --> 01:13:48,838
dressed this morning?
-Oh, oh, put -- no.

2048
01:13:48,872 --> 01:13:50,115
-[Laughs]

2049
01:13:51,634 --> 01:13:53,774
-Planet International Falls.

2050
01:13:56,949 --> 01:13:58,710
-Oh! Here he is again!
-What the...

2051
01:13:58,744 --> 01:14:02,610
-They're just ignoring the fact
they have a giant out there.

2052
01:14:02,645 --> 01:14:04,750
-Your USC losers!

2053
01:14:04,785 --> 01:14:08,754
-Just in case, tell the giant
he'd better keep awake tonight.

2054
01:14:08,789 --> 01:14:10,687
-Huh?
-You never know.

2055
01:14:10,722 --> 01:14:12,275
He might get through
those meteorites.

2056
01:14:12,309 --> 01:14:13,932
-Bawk, bah, bah, bah, bawk.

2057
01:14:13,966 --> 01:14:15,589
-Bring those Earthlings
into the Great Hall.

2058
01:14:15,623 --> 01:14:16,866
-Right.

2059
01:14:16,900 --> 01:14:19,075
-Well, time for our daily
empty threats session.

2060
01:14:21,457 --> 01:14:23,044
-Krankor will be with you
in a few moments.

2061
01:14:23,079 --> 01:14:24,632
Uh, appointments
kind of backed up today.

2062
01:14:24,667 --> 01:14:28,740
You can have a seat there.

2063
01:14:28,774 --> 01:14:29,741
-Sit down.

2064
01:14:29,775 --> 01:14:32,364
Hey, sit down!

2065
01:14:32,398 --> 01:14:33,503
Sit down, I told you!

2066
01:14:33,538 --> 01:14:34,884
-Come on, this
is getting embarrassing!

2067
01:14:34,918 --> 01:14:35,850
-Hey, what do I have to do?

2068
01:14:35,885 --> 01:14:37,058
I told you to sit down!

2069
01:14:37,093 --> 01:14:39,198
-Oh, he knocked him
slightly off balance!

2070
01:14:39,233 --> 01:14:40,268
-This must be reported

2071
01:14:40,303 --> 01:14:45,273
to Amnesty International,
or the USDA.

2072
01:14:45,308 --> 01:14:46,723
-Heh, heh!

2073
01:14:46,758 --> 01:14:48,035
Maybe you'll listen to me now.

2074
01:14:48,069 --> 01:14:52,488
-Chickens are a cruel people.

2075
01:14:52,522 --> 01:14:53,627
♪♪

2076
01:14:53,661 --> 01:14:55,491
-[Clears throat] Okay.
Who called this meeting?

2077
01:14:55,525 --> 01:14:56,802
-I didn't.
-I didn't, no.

2078
01:14:56,837 --> 01:14:58,424
-Can we go?

2079
01:14:58,459 --> 01:15:01,427
♪♪

2080
01:15:01,462 --> 01:15:04,465
-I didn't see you.

2081
01:15:04,500 --> 01:15:05,535
Whoa!

2082
01:15:05,570 --> 01:15:08,987
-Get the DeSoto started.

2083
01:15:09,021 --> 01:15:11,127
-Hey, what's that?
A rocket!

2084
01:15:11,161 --> 01:15:12,300
-Oh!

2085
01:15:12,335 --> 01:15:14,613
-Oh, no, it's just
ductwork, okay.

2086
01:15:19,894 --> 01:15:20,964
-Oh.

2087
01:15:20,999 --> 01:15:23,933
-Krankor is
Mary, Queen of Scots.

2088
01:15:23,967 --> 01:15:25,106
-Taxi!

2089
01:15:25,141 --> 01:15:27,523
[All chuckle]

2090
01:15:27,557 --> 01:15:29,076
-Go ahead on three.

2091
01:15:30,249 --> 01:15:31,975
-Oh, ho!

2092
01:15:32,010 --> 01:15:34,564
-Oh?
-Oh, please, not this!

2093
01:15:34,599 --> 01:15:36,842
Anything but an old
Star Trek set!

2094
01:15:39,949 --> 01:15:43,608
-Here you see Krankor,
a part of my domain

2095
01:15:43,642 --> 01:15:46,576
which no man has ever seen.

2096
01:15:46,611 --> 01:15:49,752
It is the last thingwhich you will see in this life.

2097
01:15:49,786 --> 01:15:53,203
-So how are you guys?
-What do you mean?

2098
01:15:53,238 --> 01:15:54,308
What do you mean by that?

2099
01:15:54,342 --> 01:15:56,897
-Look!
-Look!

2100
01:15:56,931 --> 01:15:58,174
-What's that?

2101
01:15:58,208 --> 01:16:01,108
-Cecil Fielder!

2102
01:16:01,142 --> 01:16:02,247
-You see that?

2103
01:16:02,281 --> 01:16:03,800
-What the devil is that?

2104
01:16:03,835 --> 01:16:05,284
-It's the monster
which guards this place.

2105
01:16:05,319 --> 01:16:07,252
-Did you hear that?
A monster!

2106
01:16:07,286 --> 01:16:08,149
-A monster?

2107
01:16:08,184 --> 01:16:09,634
-Quite right, my dear Macken,

2108
01:16:09,668 --> 01:16:11,636
a monster which I created.

2109
01:16:11,670 --> 01:16:13,361
He obeys my slightest command.

2110
01:16:13,396 --> 01:16:16,226
-Like wander around aimlessly
and gain weight.

2111
01:16:16,261 --> 01:16:18,401
Yeah!

2112
01:16:18,435 --> 01:16:20,610
-The guardian has moved
into position.

2113
01:16:20,645 --> 01:16:23,130
All persons are warned
to stay clear of him.

2114
01:16:23,164 --> 01:16:24,131
-Very good.

2115
01:16:24,165 --> 01:16:25,442
-Give yourself a star.

2116
01:16:25,477 --> 01:16:27,410
-Now, gentlemen,
your time has come.

2117
01:16:27,444 --> 01:16:29,136
Prepare to leave Krankor.

2118
01:16:29,170 --> 01:16:30,309
-What's that?

2119
01:16:30,344 --> 01:16:32,001
-Prepare to leave.

2120
01:16:32,035 --> 01:16:33,071
-This is not happening.

2121
01:16:33,105 --> 01:16:36,350
-Each of you will enter
a space capsule.

2122
01:16:36,384 --> 01:16:37,869
-What?

2123
01:16:37,903 --> 01:16:42,321
-Each of you will enter
a space capsule!

2124
01:16:42,356 --> 01:16:43,702
-It will be sealed up.

2125
01:16:43,737 --> 01:16:45,531
Each one of you, in turn
will then blast off...

2126
01:16:45,566 --> 01:16:46,567
-What's that?

2127
01:16:46,602 --> 01:16:47,603
-...and travel far, far out...

2128
01:16:47,637 --> 01:16:48,914
-What'd he say?

2129
01:16:48,949 --> 01:16:50,295
-Come again?

2130
01:16:50,329 --> 01:16:51,434
-Your course will be selected
at random...

2131
01:16:51,468 --> 01:16:52,677
-What?
-No?

2132
01:16:52,711 --> 01:16:54,264
-...and will ultimately
be determined

2133
01:16:54,299 --> 01:16:56,025
by the celestial bodies
near which you pass.

2134
01:16:56,059 --> 01:16:57,923
-What'd he say?
-Those of you who are fortunate

2135
01:16:57,958 --> 01:16:59,476
will fall into a star.

2136
01:16:59,511 --> 01:17:01,651
-How's that?
-Your agony will be horrible,

2137
01:17:01,686 --> 01:17:02,583
but it will be brief.

2138
01:17:02,618 --> 01:17:03,757
-Beg pardon?

2139
01:17:03,791 --> 01:17:05,379
-The first rocket will be
manned by Dr. Macken.

2140
01:17:05,413 --> 01:17:07,036
-You know, wouldn't it be
cheaper and quicker

2141
01:17:07,070 --> 01:17:09,417
to just bludgeon them
right here?

2142
01:17:09,452 --> 01:17:10,867
-Efficiency.

2143
01:17:10,902 --> 01:17:13,007
-No!
-Oh!

2144
01:17:13,042 --> 01:17:14,422
♪♪

2145
01:17:14,457 --> 01:17:16,010
-Why, Dr. Macken,
you surprise me.

2146
01:17:16,045 --> 01:17:18,047
-I thought you were
a total puss!

2147
01:17:18,081 --> 01:17:19,151
-You look so glum.

2148
01:17:19,186 --> 01:17:21,706
After all, you preferred
not to surrender.

2149
01:17:21,740 --> 01:17:24,087
[Laughs]

2150
01:17:24,122 --> 01:17:27,850
-Hey, hey, hey!
Don't moon me over there, hey!

2151
01:17:27,884 --> 01:17:29,645
-Yep, agonizing death.

2152
01:17:29,679 --> 01:17:34,132
No doubt about it, yeah.

2153
01:17:34,166 --> 01:17:36,099
-Sir, we only have two ships.
Can we double up?

2154
01:17:36,134 --> 01:17:37,307
-What?

2155
01:17:37,342 --> 01:17:38,757
The Prince of Space?

2156
01:17:38,792 --> 01:17:39,620
-He's coming!
-Huh?

2157
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:41,035
-Oh!
-Prince of Space!

2158
01:17:41,070 --> 01:17:42,727
Prince of Space is coming!

2159
01:17:42,761 --> 01:17:44,660
-Tickets at all
Ticketmaster outlets.

2160
01:17:44,694 --> 01:17:47,110
-Oh, there he is!

2161
01:17:47,145 --> 01:17:49,768
-What?
-Hi, be right with you.

2162
01:17:49,803 --> 01:17:50,873
Whoa!
Whoa, whoa.

2163
01:17:50,907 --> 01:17:51,943
-What a fool.

2164
01:17:51,977 --> 01:17:53,289
-He has defeated us
numerous times.

2165
01:17:53,323 --> 01:17:54,635
What makes him think
he can do it again?

2166
01:17:54,670 --> 01:17:57,086
-The guardian will make
mincemeat out of him.

2167
01:17:57,120 --> 01:17:59,778
He'd smash that miserable fool
once and for all!

2168
01:17:59,813 --> 01:18:03,679
-♪ In the land of Dairy Queen

2169
01:18:06,854 --> 01:18:08,511
-We're closed.

2170
01:18:12,066 --> 01:18:14,793
-He looks like a welder
who has fainting spells.

2171
01:18:17,037 --> 01:18:18,314
-Ross Perot!

2172
01:18:18,348 --> 01:18:20,696
-This is starting to be
kind of a weird movie.

2173
01:18:20,730 --> 01:18:23,043
-Mm-hmm, yeah.
-Ah.

2174
01:18:23,077 --> 01:18:25,459
-Ah, he kills with
an enormous air burp.

2175
01:18:27,703 --> 01:18:31,189
-Um, what was that
supposed to do?

2176
01:18:31,223 --> 01:18:34,226
-It's Pat!
-All right.

2177
01:18:34,261 --> 01:18:35,365
Took a look at the manual here.

2178
01:18:35,400 --> 01:18:36,642
There's giants.

2179
01:18:36,677 --> 01:18:39,473
Ah, big-eared matronly giants,
page 12.

2180
01:18:42,856 --> 01:18:44,271
-Ah.

2181
01:18:44,305 --> 01:18:47,584
-Mrs. Robinson,
are you trying to seduce me?

2182
01:18:48,585 --> 01:18:51,381
-Bless you.

2183
01:18:51,416 --> 01:18:53,659
-Hmm? What?

2184
01:18:53,694 --> 01:18:54,660
-Shh.

2185
01:18:54,695 --> 01:18:56,490
-Huh? No, not today.

2186
01:18:58,941 --> 01:19:01,840
-Some monsters just should
not wear belts.

2187
01:19:01,875 --> 01:19:03,531
-[Chuckles]

2188
01:19:03,566 --> 01:19:08,329
♪♪

2189
01:19:08,364 --> 01:19:10,469
-Ooh, he's a yam with features.

2190
01:19:13,956 --> 01:19:16,234
-He's going to Ultrabrite him
to death.

2191
01:19:18,823 --> 01:19:22,033
-♪ What would you say
if I sang out of tune ♪

2192
01:19:26,554 --> 01:19:29,143
-Now I'll circle in
and get at some of that plaque.

2193
01:19:37,151 --> 01:19:38,325
-Attention, gunners --

2194
01:19:38,359 --> 01:19:40,499
Blast him with every
available battery!

2195
01:19:40,534 --> 01:19:43,157
Automatic flak and fire!

2196
01:19:43,192 --> 01:19:44,814
-Okay. A little of this,
a little of that.

2197
01:19:44,849 --> 01:19:46,160
Strike-ups this over here.

2198
01:19:46,195 --> 01:19:47,541
[Gunfire]

2199
01:19:47,575 --> 01:19:48,818
-Ooh!

2200
01:19:48,853 --> 01:19:50,164
Is this worth a "ha, ha"?

2201
01:19:50,199 --> 01:19:51,545
Nah, I'll save it.

2202
01:19:52,857 --> 01:19:54,341
-Eh, ha, ha.

2203
01:19:54,375 --> 01:19:55,342
-Oh, I guess.

2204
01:19:55,376 --> 01:19:57,206
-Ha, ha, ha!

2205
01:19:57,240 --> 01:19:59,622
So much for that
Prince of Space!

2206
01:19:59,656 --> 01:20:01,003
Nothing, not even he,

2207
01:20:01,037 --> 01:20:03,971
could resist the devastating
effect of my thorium bombs!

2208
01:20:04,006 --> 01:20:05,110
-What?

2209
01:20:05,145 --> 01:20:07,285
-Now, let's get on
with our ceremony, eh?

2210
01:20:07,319 --> 01:20:08,493
Ha, ha, ha!

2211
01:20:08,527 --> 01:20:09,597
-No thanks.

2212
01:20:09,632 --> 01:20:10,806
Does he realize
how forced it sounds?

2213
01:20:10,840 --> 01:20:14,430
-Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha,
ha, ha, ha, ha!

2214
01:20:14,464 --> 01:20:15,845
-Ugh, those eggs.

2215
01:20:15,880 --> 01:20:17,364
-All right, Macken.
You're first.

2216
01:20:17,398 --> 01:20:18,537
Get a move on!

2217
01:20:20,332 --> 01:20:22,645
-No!
-Dr. Macken, no!

2218
01:20:22,679 --> 01:20:24,198
-Now we isolate
our first contestant

2219
01:20:24,233 --> 01:20:25,648
in a soundproof booth.

2220
01:20:25,682 --> 01:20:27,236
-Hey!
-Get back here!

2221
01:20:27,270 --> 01:20:28,306
-What are you doing?

2222
01:20:28,340 --> 01:20:29,376
[All shouting]

2223
01:20:29,410 --> 01:20:30,515
-What?

2224
01:20:30,549 --> 01:20:31,688
-Another beer here.

2225
01:20:33,104 --> 01:20:35,761
[Laser guns fire]

2226
01:20:35,796 --> 01:20:37,694
-Back to my dried good stores.

2227
01:20:41,940 --> 01:20:43,459
-Seeing these guys,
it's hard to believe

2228
01:20:43,493 --> 01:20:45,461
human beings ever have sex.

2229
01:20:45,495 --> 01:20:48,188
[Laser gunfire]

2230
01:20:48,222 --> 01:20:49,810
-[Gasps]

2231
01:20:49,845 --> 01:20:50,846
-Oh!
-He wasn't killed!

2232
01:20:50,880 --> 01:20:52,709
-What?

2233
01:20:52,744 --> 01:20:57,059
-Um, hello?

2234
01:20:57,093 --> 01:20:58,232
-Prince of Space,

2235
01:20:58,267 --> 01:20:59,889
you're still alive, are you?

2236
01:20:59,924 --> 01:21:01,649
-Of course I am!

2237
01:21:01,684 --> 01:21:03,237
And I will keep fighting

2238
01:21:03,272 --> 01:21:06,068
to protect the people
who call upon me

2239
01:21:06,102 --> 01:21:08,794
to save them
from your domination.

2240
01:21:08,829 --> 01:21:10,072
-Blast him!

2241
01:21:10,106 --> 01:21:12,108
♪♪

2242
01:21:12,143 --> 01:21:14,455
-I didn't say blast,
I said, "rest him, rest him!"

2243
01:21:14,490 --> 01:21:15,905
-Listen.
-Is that the door?

2244
01:21:15,940 --> 01:21:19,667
-I call upon you to surrender,
to release these Earthlings,

2245
01:21:19,702 --> 01:21:22,601
to return them to wherever
you took them from,

2246
01:21:22,636 --> 01:21:25,432
and to cease your evil
plotting once and for all!

2247
01:21:25,466 --> 01:21:27,123
-You can't see me!

2248
01:21:27,158 --> 01:21:28,849
A-ha, ha.

2249
01:21:28,884 --> 01:21:33,992
♪♪

2250
01:21:34,027 --> 01:21:34,924
-Come out, Professor.

2251
01:21:34,959 --> 01:21:36,270
-Prince of Space!

2252
01:21:36,305 --> 01:21:38,583
-It's Michael Jeter.
Of course it's Prince of Space!

2253
01:21:45,935 --> 01:21:49,628
-Oh, our collective headaches!

2254
01:21:49,663 --> 01:21:50,733
-Mouse Trap!

2255
01:21:50,767 --> 01:21:52,252
♪ Duh-da, da, da, da, rink,
da, dum ♪

2256
01:21:52,286 --> 01:21:53,253
-♪ Do, do, do, do-do-do

2257
01:21:53,287 --> 01:21:58,258
♪♪

2258
01:21:59,155 --> 01:22:01,192
-You, turn on the reserve power.-Right.

2259
01:22:01,226 --> 01:22:03,125
-Switch on the heating current
to that griddle.

2260
01:22:03,159 --> 01:22:04,816
-All right.
-Now that I've got him,

2261
01:22:04,850 --> 01:22:06,024
I'm going to boil him alive.

2262
01:22:06,059 --> 01:22:07,267
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

2263
01:22:07,301 --> 01:22:09,925
-Weird me out.

2264
01:22:09,959 --> 01:22:14,308
-I hope he has his tanning
goggles on, ha, ha!

2265
01:22:14,343 --> 01:22:18,071
-Here comes the deadly
fly rod cases.

2266
01:22:18,105 --> 01:22:19,313
-Dearly beloved,
we are gathered here

2267
01:22:19,348 --> 01:22:21,281
to get through
this thing called life.

2268
01:22:24,801 --> 01:22:28,460
-Careful, sweetie, no railing.

2269
01:22:28,495 --> 01:22:32,637
-Gentleman, prepare to be
Super Soaked!

2270
01:22:32,671 --> 01:22:37,504
-No one can resist my,
uh, things.

2271
01:22:37,538 --> 01:22:40,990
-Rapid deployment system
leaves no time to react!

2272
01:22:41,025 --> 01:22:42,233
-And then...

2273
01:22:42,267 --> 01:22:45,132
-Yeah, the finger coming out.

2274
01:22:45,167 --> 01:22:48,515
-Come on out, varmint!

2275
01:22:48,549 --> 01:22:51,621
-Shouldn't have let Mom
make my costume.

2276
01:22:51,656 --> 01:22:56,109
Oh, I am saving up
such a laugh.

2277
01:22:56,143 --> 01:22:57,731
-He's well-cooked.

2278
01:22:57,765 --> 01:22:58,835
Enough!
-Right.

2279
01:23:01,528 --> 01:23:03,875
-Steamed Prince of Space,
or fried in beer batter?

2280
01:23:03,909 --> 01:23:05,946
-Ah, Prince is alive!
-Dope.

2281
01:23:05,981 --> 01:23:08,742
I was hiding here, ya...

2282
01:23:08,776 --> 01:23:09,846
-Enough of this.

2283
01:23:09,881 --> 01:23:11,020
When will you ever learn?

2284
01:23:11,055 --> 01:23:12,297
Your guns won't work on me.

2285
01:23:12,332 --> 01:23:13,781
-The giant!
-Aah!

2286
01:23:13,816 --> 01:23:15,956
-Brilliant new plan, Sir.

2287
01:23:17,578 --> 01:23:20,202
-Fire lasers!

2288
01:23:20,236 --> 01:23:23,032
-Come on, the movie is over.
Let's just -- let's just go.

2289
01:23:23,067 --> 01:23:25,414
-No, it's not. It's not.
-It's not.

2290
01:23:25,448 --> 01:23:27,795
-Come on.
-Okay.

2291
01:23:27,830 --> 01:23:29,832
-Put Debbie on hold for a sec.

2292
01:23:31,696 --> 01:23:32,766
-Sit down.

2293
01:23:32,800 --> 01:23:34,699
-Sick, angry, a turtle.

2294
01:23:34,733 --> 01:23:37,115
What?

2295
01:23:37,150 --> 01:23:38,668
-Well, I suppose
that's it for me.

2296
01:23:38,703 --> 01:23:39,704
Yep, I'm dead.

2297
01:23:39,738 --> 01:23:41,050
-Now, look...

2298
01:23:41,085 --> 01:23:43,052
Give up,
or I'll have to kill you.

2299
01:23:43,880 --> 01:23:45,606
-Well, I can't back that up!

2300
01:23:48,126 --> 01:23:49,438
-No!

2301
01:23:49,472 --> 01:23:50,784
-Oh, oh!

2302
01:23:50,818 --> 01:23:52,648
-You'll never defeat me!
Bye now!

2303
01:23:52,682 --> 01:23:54,236
Into the giblet-mobile!

2304
01:23:56,859 --> 01:23:58,171
-Now is our chance.
Come on, follow me!

2305
01:23:58,205 --> 01:23:59,172
-Yes.

2306
01:23:59,206 --> 01:24:01,381
-I have no
objective whatsoever.

2307
01:24:01,415 --> 01:24:03,038
-Hey, Prince,
where are you going?

2308
01:24:03,072 --> 01:24:04,349
-Follow me! Quickly.

2309
01:24:04,384 --> 01:24:07,249
Come on!
Come on, all of you!

2310
01:24:07,283 --> 01:24:09,044
-Just run potty,
and then we'll go, okay?

2311
01:24:09,078 --> 01:24:10,769
-Mike, I swear,
I am never going to forget

2312
01:24:10,804 --> 01:24:13,634
what the Japanese did to us
with this movie.

2313
01:24:13,669 --> 01:24:16,154
-Oh, come on, this way!
-No, wait! Look out!

2314
01:24:16,189 --> 01:24:17,397
-Oh?
-Oh!

2315
01:24:17,431 --> 01:24:18,398
-Oh, ow!
-Oh! Ow!

2316
01:24:18,432 --> 01:24:19,502
-We're trapped!
-Ooh!

2317
01:24:19,537 --> 01:24:20,848
-Not yet. Come, this way!

2318
01:24:20,883 --> 01:24:22,816
-No, no, wait! What? Stop.

2319
01:24:22,850 --> 01:24:24,059
Oh, ooh, ah!

2320
01:24:24,093 --> 01:24:25,646
-Oh, wait. Stop. This way!
Now run!

2321
01:24:25,681 --> 01:24:27,062
No, wait, come on!
-Oh!

2322
01:24:27,096 --> 01:24:28,546
-No, look out.
No, wait. Stop. Huh?

2323
01:24:28,580 --> 01:24:31,307
-Oh, Prince of Space?
-Oh, huh, don't stop!

2324
01:24:31,342 --> 01:24:33,033
-Hurry. Come this way!

2325
01:24:33,068 --> 01:24:34,172
-Oh, no, wait!

2326
01:24:34,207 --> 01:24:35,449
Is that the way out?

2327
01:24:35,484 --> 01:24:36,795
-Of course, come on.

2328
01:24:36,830 --> 01:24:38,970
-Wait, probably it isn't!
No, I'll follow you.

2329
01:24:39,004 --> 01:24:40,696
Wait, Prince of Space!

2330
01:24:40,730 --> 01:24:42,111
-The Ritz Brothers
had more dignity!

2331
01:24:42,146 --> 01:24:43,802
-Over here!
-No kidding.

2332
01:24:43,837 --> 01:24:45,356
[All shouting]

2333
01:24:45,390 --> 01:24:46,633
-Calm down, calm down.

2334
01:24:46,667 --> 01:24:47,806
-Calm down.

2335
01:24:47,841 --> 01:24:49,325
-Okay, now panic.

2336
01:24:49,360 --> 01:24:51,465
-Ah, ha.

2337
01:24:51,500 --> 01:24:53,018
Caught like rats in a trap!

2338
01:24:53,053 --> 01:24:56,574
You'll be safe enough here.

2339
01:24:56,608 --> 01:24:59,094
I'm leaving for Earth now,
but when I come back,

2340
01:24:59,128 --> 01:25:01,855
I'll have a very special
kind of death for you,

2341
01:25:01,889 --> 01:25:04,409
my dear Prince of Space.

2342
01:25:04,444 --> 01:25:05,514
Goodbye!

2343
01:25:05,548 --> 01:25:06,791
-So he has a quick errand

2344
01:25:06,825 --> 01:25:09,690
before he kills Prince of Space.

2345
01:25:11,554 --> 01:25:14,316
-What?
What are you looking at?

2346
01:25:14,350 --> 01:25:16,283
-I had a very good reason
for not killing him now.

2347
01:25:16,318 --> 01:25:19,148
He's going to prepare
for blastoff in his flagship,

2348
01:25:19,183 --> 01:25:21,185
and unfortunately
it's the only ship available

2349
01:25:21,219 --> 01:25:22,531
that will take you
back to Earth.

2350
01:25:22,565 --> 01:25:23,635
-Yeah.

2351
01:25:23,670 --> 01:25:25,154
-Now, all of you stay
close behind me

2352
01:25:25,189 --> 01:25:26,604
and do exactly
what I tell you to do.

2353
01:25:26,638 --> 01:25:28,295
-Oh!

2354
01:25:30,608 --> 01:25:31,850
-Okay, now watch more.

2355
01:25:31,885 --> 01:25:33,162
There you go.

2356
01:25:33,197 --> 01:25:36,683
[Laser gun firing]

2357
01:25:36,717 --> 01:25:40,100
-Little more, yes.
Good, watch him, good.

2358
01:25:40,135 --> 01:25:42,033
-My grill lighter is saving us!

2359
01:25:42,067 --> 01:25:44,380
[Sizzling]

2360
01:25:44,415 --> 01:25:46,279
-Oh, we are more
interested now.

2361
01:25:48,039 --> 01:25:50,352
-Why is he melting
semi-sweet chocolate?

2362
01:25:50,386 --> 01:25:52,699
-Hurry up now, come on!

2363
01:25:52,733 --> 01:25:54,839
-Hey, guys, wait, watch this.
Watch this.

2364
01:25:55,633 --> 01:25:56,599
-My arthritis!

2365
01:25:56,634 --> 01:25:58,014
Oh, my spastic colon!

2366
01:25:58,049 --> 01:25:59,533
-Oh, my gout!
-Oh, my bad knee!

2367
01:25:59,568 --> 01:26:00,845
-Oh, my baldness!

2368
01:26:00,879 --> 01:26:04,538
♪♪

2369
01:26:04,573 --> 01:26:06,264
-Prince of Crossing Guards!

2370
01:26:06,299 --> 01:26:08,232
♪♪

2371
01:26:08,266 --> 01:26:10,717
-Ah, ha, ha, ha, ha.

2372
01:26:10,751 --> 01:26:12,167
-Ha, ha, ha!

2373
01:26:12,201 --> 01:26:14,238
-Would you get back further,
you morons?

2374
01:26:14,272 --> 01:26:17,655
♪♪

2375
01:26:17,689 --> 01:26:19,312
Stop right where you are.

2376
01:26:19,346 --> 01:26:21,797
-It's him!
-It's the Prince of Space!

2377
01:26:21,831 --> 01:26:23,143
-Oh, I love him!
-Let's get his autograph!

2378
01:26:23,178 --> 01:26:25,145
-Come back, you fools!
He's all alone!

2379
01:26:26,284 --> 01:26:27,527
-Ah.

2380
01:26:27,561 --> 01:26:28,907
-My one stance.

2381
01:26:28,942 --> 01:26:30,150
-Stand where you are!
-And who's that?

2382
01:26:30,185 --> 01:26:31,289
-The first man who walks down
the ramp

2383
01:26:31,324 --> 01:26:32,946
will be signing
his own death warrant.

2384
01:26:32,980 --> 01:26:34,361
I booby-trapped the whole thing,

2385
01:26:34,396 --> 01:26:35,811
and your own thorium bombs

2386
01:26:35,845 --> 01:26:37,295
will blast you
into the next world!

2387
01:26:37,330 --> 01:26:38,400
-Oh!
-Oh?

2388
01:26:38,434 --> 01:26:39,470
-You lie.

2389
01:26:39,504 --> 01:26:40,609
-You can find out pretty easily

2390
01:26:40,643 --> 01:26:41,886
whether I'm
telling you the truth.

2391
01:26:41,920 --> 01:26:44,060
Look behind you
in that corridor.

2392
01:26:44,095 --> 01:26:45,234
-What?

2393
01:26:45,269 --> 01:26:46,891
-Oh, gross, right on the rug!

2394
01:26:46,925 --> 01:26:49,134
-All right.
Then I surrender.

2395
01:26:49,721 --> 01:26:50,998
-They lapped themselves.

2396
01:26:51,033 --> 01:26:52,310
-Get back!
Get out of sight!

2397
01:26:52,345 --> 01:26:53,725
-Capture them for hostages!

2398
01:26:53,760 --> 01:26:54,968
♪♪

2399
01:26:55,002 --> 01:26:59,179
-They have no accumulated
memory whatsoever!

2400
01:26:59,214 --> 01:27:03,010
-Come on, why don't you try
to board your ship?

2401
01:27:03,045 --> 01:27:04,011
-Why, you...

2402
01:27:04,046 --> 01:27:05,979
-Now your breath is bad too!

2403
01:27:06,013 --> 01:27:07,636
-Oh, Prince,
the hall is being --

2404
01:27:07,670 --> 01:27:09,120
-Are we grateful to see you!

2405
01:27:09,154 --> 01:27:10,742
Say you're all right, please.
-Are you all right?

2406
01:27:10,777 --> 01:27:12,986
-Quiet down!
We haven't a moment to lose.

2407
01:27:13,020 --> 01:27:14,263
Everybody,
board this ship right away.

2408
01:27:14,298 --> 01:27:15,471
-Well, what about you?

2409
01:27:15,506 --> 01:27:17,197
-I will stay here until
you're safe on your way.

2410
01:27:17,232 --> 01:27:18,336
[Crashes]
-What's that?

2411
01:27:18,371 --> 01:27:19,372
-Go on, hurry!

2412
01:27:19,406 --> 01:27:20,787
-Oh, uh!
-Yes!

2413
01:27:20,821 --> 01:27:23,859
-Next, the Prince will sew
name tags in their underwear,

2414
01:27:23,893 --> 01:27:25,447
bunch of babies.

2415
01:27:25,481 --> 01:27:28,381
-Yeah, I need those guys like
I need another 1-inch wiener.

2416
01:27:28,415 --> 01:27:30,900
♪♪

2417
01:27:30,935 --> 01:27:31,970
-Keep pushing, men.

2418
01:27:32,005 --> 01:27:33,696
We're almost out
of our atmosphere.

2419
01:27:33,731 --> 01:27:36,147
♪♪

2420
01:27:36,181 --> 01:27:40,358
[Panting]

2421
01:27:40,393 --> 01:27:42,774
[Crashing]

2422
01:27:42,809 --> 01:27:45,708
-My coop!
My beautiful, beautiful coop!

2423
01:27:45,743 --> 01:27:47,054
Oh, ho!

2424
01:27:47,089 --> 01:27:48,953
-Wah, bawk, bawk, bawk.

2425
01:27:48,987 --> 01:27:50,644
-Bawk!
-Bah!

2426
01:27:50,679 --> 01:27:52,646
♪♪

2427
01:27:52,681 --> 01:27:54,027
-If they'd built
this up to code,

2428
01:27:54,061 --> 01:27:57,099
this never would have happened!

2429
01:27:57,133 --> 01:27:59,101
-Ah, yes,
the ancient Japanese tradition

2430
01:27:59,135 --> 01:28:00,827
of blowing up models
at the end of the movie!

2431
01:28:00,861 --> 01:28:04,175
-A blast at East Bedrock
claimed the lives

2432
01:28:04,209 --> 01:28:08,144
of Frederick R. Flintstone
and Barnabas Rubble today.

2433
01:28:10,388 --> 01:28:13,391
-And a proud,
noble civilization dies out,

2434
01:28:13,426 --> 01:28:14,668
sometimes.

2435
01:28:14,703 --> 01:28:18,154
This loser civilization,
however, will not be missed.

2436
01:28:20,260 --> 01:28:21,882
-Dr. Macken, Dr. Macken!

2437
01:28:21,917 --> 01:28:23,436
-I'm wet again!

2438
01:28:23,470 --> 01:28:25,300
-The automatic pilot
is working perfectly!

2439
01:28:25,334 --> 01:28:26,370
We're on a direct course
for Earth.

2440
01:28:26,404 --> 01:28:27,440
-Wonderful.

2441
01:28:27,474 --> 01:28:29,096
-And look there,
on the visual screen --

2442
01:28:29,131 --> 01:28:30,615
The one we owe everything to.

2443
01:28:30,650 --> 01:28:31,616
-Oh.

2444
01:28:31,651 --> 01:28:34,895
-Ah, it's the Prince of Space!

2445
01:28:34,930 --> 01:28:36,172
He wouldn't even let us
say thanks.

2446
01:28:36,207 --> 01:28:37,450
Who knows if we'll ever
see him again.

2447
01:28:37,484 --> 01:28:38,865
-Say, we'd better radio ahead.

2448
01:28:38,899 --> 01:28:40,384
Tell the Earth we're safe,
that we're coming home

2449
01:28:40,418 --> 01:28:41,695
thanks to Prince of Space.

2450
01:28:41,730 --> 01:28:43,352
-Yeah.

2451
01:28:43,387 --> 01:28:45,181
-On their own, the giant
infant scientist

2452
01:28:45,216 --> 01:28:46,976
survived another minute
and then crashed.

2453
01:28:47,011 --> 01:28:48,909
♪♪

2454
01:28:48,944 --> 01:28:50,670
-Meanwhile,
all the boots on Earth

2455
01:28:50,704 --> 01:28:53,189
get duller and less black.

2456
01:28:53,224 --> 01:28:56,745
-And yet I feel so empty.

2457
01:28:56,779 --> 01:29:00,093
-You know, this movie made me
want to renounce my Toyota.

2458
01:29:00,127 --> 01:29:01,025
♪♪

2459
01:29:01,059 --> 01:29:03,786
-Ah!

2460
01:29:03,821 --> 01:29:05,340
-Oh, it's the end!

2461
01:29:05,374 --> 01:29:07,411
Oh, the movie can't end
enough for me!

2462
01:29:07,445 --> 01:29:10,275
-Ah, let's get into space!
-Oh, ah, this one!

2463
01:29:16,005 --> 01:29:17,628
What?

2464
01:29:22,633 --> 01:29:24,255
-Okay, okay, okay.
-Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

2465
01:29:24,289 --> 01:29:25,981
-On the Satellite of Love,
right, right?

2466
01:29:26,015 --> 01:29:27,396
-Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.
-There's no time lags.

2467
01:29:27,431 --> 01:29:29,364
Mike is not a puny little robot.

2468
01:29:29,398 --> 01:29:31,089
-Nope, nope, I...
Well, I don't think so.

2469
01:29:31,124 --> 01:29:32,884
-Because I tell you, guys,
you get to the point

2470
01:29:32,919 --> 01:29:35,266
where you just want to go,
"Wormhole, back off!"

2471
01:29:35,300 --> 01:29:38,373
-No, I hear you, but seems like
everything is back to normal.

2472
01:29:38,407 --> 01:29:40,513
Oh, you guys know my wife,
Krankor, right?

2473
01:29:40,547 --> 01:29:41,824
-Wah!
-Whoa, whoa!

2474
01:29:41,859 --> 01:29:42,963
Get me out of here!

2475
01:29:42,998 --> 01:29:46,484
-[Laughs]
-Ha, ha, ha, ha!

2476
01:29:46,519 --> 01:29:48,244
-Oh, that was good.
We got them, Krankor.

2477
01:29:48,279 --> 01:29:49,763
-We certainly got them
that time!

2478
01:29:49,798 --> 01:29:51,006
Ha!
-Yeah.

2479
01:29:51,040 --> 01:29:52,317
-Ha.

2480
01:29:52,352 --> 01:29:53,422
-Well, there's no reason
for you to hang around.

2481
01:29:53,457 --> 01:29:56,183
-You could take off.
-They ran like fools, ha!

2482
01:29:56,218 --> 01:29:57,461
-Yeah.
-Ha!

2483
01:29:57,495 --> 01:29:59,152
-Yeah, I guess
they did, Krankor.

2484
01:29:59,186 --> 01:30:01,430
-We pulled the wool
over their eyes. Ha!

2485
01:30:01,465 --> 01:30:02,535
-Wow.
-You know what, Krankor?

2486
01:30:02,569 --> 01:30:03,743
I want you to leave.
All right?

2487
01:30:03,777 --> 01:30:04,813
-Oh, do you?

2488
01:30:04,847 --> 01:30:06,124
Well, you may be interested
to know

2489
01:30:06,159 --> 01:30:07,781
that I have already
conquered your puny Satellite

2490
01:30:07,816 --> 01:30:09,093
and that you have
no defense against...

2491
01:30:09,127 --> 01:30:10,681
-Ah!
-Oh, oh, please don't hurt me!

2492
01:30:10,715 --> 01:30:12,027
No, no! Don't hit!
Don't hit! Don't hit!

2493
01:30:12,061 --> 01:30:13,373
-Well, Krankor.
-Yeah.

2494
01:30:13,408 --> 01:30:15,375
-Mike, Crow, Servo, Krankor,

2495
01:30:15,410 --> 01:30:17,273
we're orbiting a planet
that looks like Earth.

2496
01:30:17,308 --> 01:30:18,378
-Earth?
-Wow!

2497
01:30:18,413 --> 01:30:19,483
-Earth?
-I'm not sure.

2498
01:30:19,517 --> 01:30:20,553
-Really?
-Yes!

2499
01:30:20,587 --> 01:30:22,002
-It -- it is!
-I think.

2500
01:30:22,037 --> 01:30:22,900
-Oh, would you knock it off?

2501
01:30:22,934 --> 01:30:23,970
Mrs. F, how about you?

2502
01:30:24,004 --> 01:30:27,905
Do you know where we are
or when we are?

2503
01:30:27,939 --> 01:30:29,631
-I don't know, Mike.

2504
01:30:29,665 --> 01:30:31,460
There's no sign of Bobo,

2505
01:30:31,495 --> 01:30:34,843
but there are marble columns
and intricate frescoes.

2506
01:30:34,877 --> 01:30:36,948
-Evidently,
a sewage system of some sort.

2507
01:30:36,983 --> 01:30:38,294
-Could --
could it possibly be...

2508
01:30:38,329 --> 01:30:39,813
[Fanfare plays]

2509
01:30:39,848 --> 01:30:41,781
-Welcome to Roman Times.

2510
01:30:41,815 --> 01:30:43,921
-Guards, cease them.

2511
01:30:43,955 --> 01:30:47,234
[Suspenseful music plays]

2512
01:30:47,821 --> 01:30:56,554
♪♪

2513
01:30:56,589 --> 01:31:05,390
♪♪

2514
01:31:05,425 --> 01:31:14,158
♪♪

2515
01:31:14,192 --> 01:31:22,891
♪♪

2516
01:31:22,925 --> 01:31:31,658
♪♪

2517
01:31:31,693 --> 01:31:40,425
